WEBVTT

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:35.640
So? How's the view from the Bell Tree Tower, built by the power of the Suzuki Financial Group?

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:40.660
It's amazing, Sonoko! Thanks for inviting us!

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.430
You lot should show some appreciation too!

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:48.550
This opening ceremony is supposed to be strictly for those who helped build the tower!

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:49.360
Yeah!

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:50.680
It's the best!

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.070
Thank you!

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:56.070
You can sure talk. You're the one who asked us if we wanted to come in the first place!

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.950
Hey! Is it time to leave yet?

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:03.200
Why would we be leaving, Dad? We just got here!

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:07.330
How'd I end up being dragged this high up again?!

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:12.040
Dad, come over here with us! The view's great!

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:15.980
Hmph! Don't be stupid! I'm leaving!

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:17.800
Geez...

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:22.780
Besides, haven't you heard that saying? ‘Only fools and so on like high places’!{saying is actually 'fools and smoke' but Kogorou screws it up}

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.980
But the truth is that you're scared, right?

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:31.480
D-Don't be stupid! B-Being up
 this high d-doesn't bother me at all!

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.980
Then you wouldn't be scared at all if you looked at the floor, right?

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:36.490
Huh? The floor?

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:43.280
There's no floor!

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:44.900
I'm scared! I'm scared! I'm scared!

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:46.000
Hold on, Dad!

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.710
I'm scared of high places!

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:52.750
Excuse me!

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.440
That lift goes to—

00:01:55.550 --> 00:02:02.960
This lift goes to the special observation deck. Please enjoy the view from a height of 460 metres…

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.810
Get me down!

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.810
Oh, Dad...

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:13.260
I'm sorry about this, Sonoko.

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:16.820
Don't worry. This is normal for him, isn't it?

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:16.820
What's he doing?

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:20.070
Now let's enjoy the great view from the Bell Tree!

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:23.200
Hey, Sonoko, what's that building?

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:27.040
Oh, that small thing is the Asakusa Sky Court.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.960
No connection to the Suzuki Financial Group.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:33.460
Even after it's finished, it'll probably only come up to this first observation deck at the most.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.750
That's a win for the Bell Tree then.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.620
Of course!

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:43.980
Hey, have a look at that river! It's got so many bridges!

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.770
Yeah, that's Sumida River.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.660
The blue one over there is Komagata Bridge.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.570
The red one is Azuma Bridge.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.620
And that railway bridge right ahead of us is the Tohto Bell Tree Line.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:55.690
Oh! There's a train!

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:57.640
It's so cool!

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:00.220
Huh? It's stopping on the bridge...

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:05.830
It's just slowing down. Asakusa Station is right on the other side of the bridge, after all.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:07.580
That's it!

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:14.340
How about we make a miniature model of the Tohto Bell Tree Tower and its surroundings for our summer homework project?

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.470
Oh, that's a great idea!

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:20.380
It sounds fun! Conan-<i>kun</i>,
 Ai-<i>chan</i>, let's all work together!

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.730
Hey, that sounds like a lot of hard wo—

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:24.140
We'd be happy to.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.430
Yay!

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.220
Then it's decided!

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:29.160
Let's make an awesome model!

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.900
I guess it's a good thing we came here.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.870
Let's all take lots of photos!

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.270
I'll take some videos.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:38.080
I'll read up about the Bell Tree.

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:40.160
Sure! Go ahead! 

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:42.040
But I wonder if a certain <i>somebody</i> will be fine not doing any summer homework.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:44.420
I'll use these binoculars to decide how wide an area we should make for our model! 

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.700
Leave me alone.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:47.240
There! The yellow building.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.830
Oh, wow! It's amazing!

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:53.000
Oh, I see it. What a lovely building.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:57.000
This building was built 30 years ago.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:05.090
And now, with the completion of the Bell Tree Tower, the view alone is worth four stars.

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:08.330
It is definitely a five star property.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:09.940
Wow!

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:13.430
Built 30 years ago, isn't that a bit old?

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:13.430
Darling, I think this may be our lucky day!

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:16.080
I absolutely love this house!

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:19.010
I think so too, this property is...

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:26.990
What is it?

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:29.520
No, it's nothing...

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:52.100
It's a sniper! Everybody get down!

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:55.270
You're too heavy...{***recheck with BD/animanga for v2}

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:57.600
Everyone, please stay calm! 

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:02.110
Damn, everyone's panicking!

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.660
So it really was from there.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:09.160
Where's Ran?

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:11.410
All right!

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.530
Doc! Give me your car keys!

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:16.020
My car keys?

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.940
I'm gonna go get my skateboard.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:20.540
Doc, you're too heavy...

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:23.460
Oh, wait!

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:25.300
Everyone, please stay calm!

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:27.800
Conan-<i>kun</i>...

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:02.540
I'm Shin'ichi Kudō, a high school detective.

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:06.510
While at an amusement park with my childhood friend and classmate, Ran Mouri,

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:10.010
I witnessed a suspicious deal involving a man in black.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:17.290
Since I was so focused on watching the deal, I didn't realise his partner was sneaking up from behind me.


00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:23.270
He forced me to consume poison, and when I came to...

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:26.280
...my body had shrunk!

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:29.150
If those men learnt that Shin'ichi Kudō was still alive,

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:32.530
they'd come back to finish me off, endangering everyone around me.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:36.450
At Dr. Agasa's suggestion, I hid my identity,

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:40.210
and when Ran asked my name,
 I blurted out ‘Conan Edogawa’.

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:46.350
To find out more about those guys, I ended up living with Ran and her detective father.

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:59.050
The enigmatic Black Organisation...

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:03.730
I'm not the only one who's secretly working to find out their identity.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:07.440
The Federal Bureau of Investigation — the FBI.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:11.740
James Black, André Camel, Jodie Starling...

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:14.500
And Shūichi Akai.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:22.140
He was the sharpest agent at the FBI, and an expert marksman, but then a CIA agent that had infiltrated the organisation went and...

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:26.500
And also, some new characters.

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:32.510
Masumi Sera. She transferred into the same class as Ran and I, and calls herself a detective.

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:42.520
And finally, Subaru Okiya. An engineering post-graduate university student, who is living in my empty house.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:44.020
But his identity is really...

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:46.690
My body shrunk, but my mind didn't!

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:48.860
I'm still an undefeated great detective!

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:54.820
There's always only one truth!

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:14.260
Sniping someone that accurately from so far away... Don't tell me that <i>they're</i> behind it?!

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:17.390
I have to know for sure!

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:19.310
I think this was the way to that building…

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:25.470
Oh no!

00:08:43.530 --> 00:08:44.160
What?

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:49.630
A boy fell in!

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:56.690
This goes right next to the building!

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.680
There it is! All right!

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:18.990
He couldn't have gone too far…

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:26.390
To escape without getting caught in traffic, he'd need to walk or go by bike.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:29.670
Could that be him?

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:32.380
That size and thickness...

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:34.420
It must be! That's a rifle bag!

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:41.930
Haibara, can you hear me?

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:44.890
Damn, this piece of junk!

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:48.150
Haibara! Haibara! Answer me, Haibara!

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:51.940
What is it? I'm getting a lot of static, where are you?

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:54.750
I'm chasing what I think is the sniper's bike!

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:56.770
Doctor! Call the police!

00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:57.990
Huh? Right...

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:03.410
The number plate's ‘Shinjuku Se 3317’! He's heading north on Mitsumedōri!

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:05.660
He turned left!

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.660
Damn, you're not getting away!

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:10.940
What is it? Edogawa-<i>kun</i>, are you okay?

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:13.920
Yeah, I'm just crossing Kototoi Bridge over the Sumida—

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:18.620
Damn, was that the badge's limit?!

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.390
Oh no! I'm in a blind spot!

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:36.820
Where is he?!

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:44.330
Heading the wrong way up a one-way street? It couldn't be!

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:48.460
Look out!

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.430
This is like Yaiba!{Yaiber?***}

00:10:56.610 --> 00:10:59.550
Damn, did he notice me after all?!

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:40.220
What the hell are you— I mean, what are you doing here, Sera-<i>neechan</i>?

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:44.430
I'll explain later! Let's go!

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:51.940
The number plate of the suspect's bike is ‘Shinjuku Se 3317’.

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:57.570
According to the latest report, he has crossed Kototoi Bridge, and is heading south along Sumida River.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:01.570
All cars currently on patrol nearby, head to the scene immediately! Arrest him!

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:12.960
What? You were at the Bell Tree?

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:18.710
I was following the man that was shot. As a detective.

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.050
Then you were there when it happened, weren't you?

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:24.280
Yeah. I never thought he'd be murdered.

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:27.230
I see him! Hold on tight!

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:27.510
Right!

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:39.320
He's turned left off National Route 6 and headed onto Kuramae Bridge!{***recheck with BD/animanga} Block him in from both sides!

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:42.070
Roger. All sealed off here.

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:33.900
Damn! Hold on, we're going after him!

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:37.170
No, provoking him further is too dangerous.

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:41.670
Don't worry. I'll know where he's headed soon enough.

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:51.760
He stopped.

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:56.180
He might have another getaway vehicle there.

00:13:56.180 --> 00:13:58.310
This is bad... Let's hurry!

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:00.900
Yeah. But be careful!

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:04.030
I know! We're just going to check!

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:14.290
...fleeing on a bike with the number plate Shinjuku Se 3317,{***recheck with BD/animanga} currently headed south along the Sumida River...

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.780
It appears he headed this way.

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:13.540
Right.

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:31.790
That bike!

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:33.730
Yeah. That's it.

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:35.930
So he went on foot from here...

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:53.240
Damn...

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:54.500
Sera!

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:55.850
Hey, Sera!

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:14.390
Agent Camel!

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:33.700
You're mine!

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:37.450
Bring it on!

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:53.810
Ouch…

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:55.920
Are you okay, Sera-<i>neechan</i>?

00:15:55.920 --> 00:15:57.350
Y-Yeah...

00:15:57.350 --> 00:16:00.010
If I didn't have this, I'd be dead for sure...

00:16:00.010 --> 00:16:03.240
Looks like neither of you are hurt.

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:05.940
Never mind that, are you okay, Agent Camel?

00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:07.870
No problem.

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:10.010
I was wearing this.

00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:11.070
I see.

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:13.380
But about Jodie-<i>san</i>'s gun...

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:15.700
Keep it a secret, right?

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:20.830
It's no use. He got away.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:25.480
It can't be helped. Let's leave the rest to the Japanese police.

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:28.840
I'll tell them to search the cliffs near the bay right away.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:29.460
Right.

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:32.840
Well, it's going to be hard to arrest him.

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:36.470
The sea's like a garden for the SEALs.

00:16:37.320 --> 00:16:38.850
SEALs?

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:45.600
Have a look at this.

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:51.690
From the photos we have obtained and his sniping technique, we believe the sniper to be this person.

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:54.950
Timothy Hunter, 37...

00:16:54.950 --> 00:17:01.950
A former sniper in the Navy's Special Ops squad ‘Navy SEALs’, who fought in the war in the Middle East for three years from 2003.

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:06.180
He's a war hero who accomplished many great deeds.

00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:07.750
So why would a hero do this?

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:11.480
We believe the reason to be this, the Silver Star.

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:13.300
The Silver Star?

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:20.720
It's a medal of honour awarded to soldiers who have shown gallantry in action against an enemy of the United States.{lit: bravery in a battle against a hostile armed group}

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:25.520
Hunter was awarded this medal of heroism in 2005,

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:29.740
but the next year, he was stripped of it on suspicion of violating the Rules of Engagement.

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:30.650
Stripped of it?

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:37.600
Yes. An Army officer put in a complaint saying that he shot an unarmed civilian.

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:44.290
Of course, Hunter denied it, and the case didn't go to court due to lack of evidence,

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:51.260
but that one case took him from being called the ‘Battlefield Hero’ to the ‘Suspected Hero’.

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:59.590
And perhaps due to being stripped of his Silver Star,

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:04.180
 when he returned to the war zone, Hunter had lost his usual calm, and alone on the battlefield…

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:07.310
…took an enemy bullet to his head.

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:12.230
Oh no...

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:13.620
Then what happened to Hunter?

00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:16.950
Luckily, the surgery was successful, and his life was saved.

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:19.700
But he was discharged due to his wounds.

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:24.420
He returned to America, but his misfortune didn't end there.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:29.960
Seeking a peaceful life back in America, he moved to the countryside of Seattle, Washington,

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:37.340
but his terrible memories of the warzone never left him, and have pained him ever since.

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:44.060
But his misfortune still wasn't satisfied, and extended to his wife and sister living with him.

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:46.640
He was bankrupted by a flawed investment.

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:51.860
His sister committed suicide due to being abandoned by her fiancé, and his wife died from taking an overdose.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:59.000
Hunter lost his honour, his fortune and his beloved family one after another. {Needs split}

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:04.070
Then we have no knowledge of his whereabouts for the next six years.

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:09.020
Why is he a suspect in this murder?

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:11.250
Because of what happened three weeks ago.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:18.340
Brian Woods, a reporter for a local newspaper in Seattle, was sniped with a rifle and died.

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:21.720
When the police investigated that victim,

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:26.350
they found that he'd been hounding Hunter and his wife while writing a series of articles on the ‘Suspected Hero’,

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:31.350
and had driven them both to have mental breakdowns.

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:41.200
Because of that, the police and FBI investigated Hunter as a suspect, and found he entered Japan two weeks ago.

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:48.550
And so, since we were on holiday in Japan,
 FBI HQ contacted us and ordered us to arrest him.

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:51.710
I see. And that brings us up to now.

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:55.590
Yes. By the way, what about
 Hunter's whereabouts since then?

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:59.520
We've been searching the bay, but we haven't found any real clues yet...

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:01.220
That's no surprise.

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:09.920
As you know, the the ‘SEAL’ in SEALs was taken from ‘sea’, ‘air’, and ‘land’, and swimming is supposed to be one of their talents.

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:12.730
Another of which is sniping with a rifle.

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:19.600
As for the sniping, we discovered some strange items from the roof of the building suspected to be the sniping position.

00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:20.650
Strange items?

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:21.750
Chiba-<i>kun</i>.

00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:22.900
Right.

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:25.910
In the space for the window cleaning rails on the side facing the Bell Tree Tower,

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:30.250
we found a die and a 51 mm bullet shell.

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:35.750
The shell has the same calibre as the 7.62 mm bullet used in the crime.

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:42.100
It also matches the NATO bullets used by the MK11, Hunter's favourite rifle.

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:43.100
Then it was him...?

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:50.010
About this die... Was there a die left with the shell at the sniping position in the Seattle case as well?

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:56.980
No, I haven't heard about anything like a die being found there, but there <i>is</i> a connection between Hunter and dice.

00:20:56.980 --> 00:21:02.740
Hunter loved playing dice games, and has a tattoo of dice here on his left arm.

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:04.480
I-I see.

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:10.620
It's a tenuous connection, but it means Hunter could be trying to leave some sort of message with this die.

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:18.290
Yes. And the greatest piece of evidence that Hunter was behind this lies with the victim.

00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:24.550
You mean that Hunter had a definite motive for murdering Fujinami-<i>san</i>?

00:21:24.550 --> 00:21:25.830
Yes.

00:21:25.830 --> 00:21:33.560
Seven years ago, Hiroaki Fujinami sold Hunter substandard Japanese property, and is responsible for bankrupting him.

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:34.830
What?!

00:21:34.830 --> 00:21:35.390
Then that's why...?

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:39.030
That means Hunter's the culprit for sure.

00:21:39.140 --> 00:21:43.400
Speaking of Fujinami-<i>san</i>, why
 was Sera-<i>neechan</i> tailing him?

00:21:43.710 --> 00:21:45.110
That's right...

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:46.400
Why were you tailing Fujinami-<i>san</i>?

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:51.530
A relative of a classmate of mine was thinking about marrying Fujinami,

00:21:51.530 --> 00:21:55.540
but she thought he was involved in something fishy, so she asked me to conduct a background check on him.

00:21:55.540 --> 00:22:01.040
And during my investigation I found out about Fujinami swindling good-natured foreigners

00:21:56.880 --> 00:22:00.580
You doing a background check?! Some nerve... 

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:03.930
by selling them substandard Japanese property.

00:22:03.930 --> 00:22:06.420
Right, even back then...

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:10.220
Well, it's awful that he was murdered,

00:22:10.220 --> 00:22:14.350
but it's good in the sense that the relative isn't interested in getting remarried anymore.

00:22:15.380 --> 00:22:21.150
Oh, that's right. From what you've said, I doubt this will be the end of Hunter's crime spree.

00:22:21.150 --> 00:22:22.910
Yes, you're right.

00:22:22.910 --> 00:22:26.710
Is there anyone else that Hunter might want dead?

00:22:26.710 --> 00:22:28.410
Jodie-<i>kun</i>, the photos.

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:29.160
Right.

00:22:29.630 --> 00:22:34.650
The FBI believe there are at
 least three people he may be after.

00:22:34.650 --> 00:22:36.980
T-Three people?!

00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:42.500
Yes. We believe he is likely to
 try and murder these three people.

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:50.510
Jack Waltz, 45. He's the former Army captain who reported that Hunter violated the Rules of Engagement.

00:22:50.510 --> 00:22:55.520
He currently runs a factory making military equipment in San Diego.

00:22:55.520 --> 00:22:58.690
Next, Bill Murphy, 35.

00:22:58.690 --> 00:23:05.440
He's a former Army sergeant who worked under Waltz, and was a witness to Hunter's violation of the Rules of Engagement.

00:23:05.440 --> 00:23:08.860
After being discharged, he joined
 Waltz's company as a secretary.

00:23:08.860 --> 00:23:11.810
I guess he can't murder them if they're in San Diego.

00:23:11.810 --> 00:23:16.200
No, they're both currently in Japan.

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:17.340
What?!

00:23:17.340 --> 00:23:23.630
Waltz arrived in Kyōto with his family two days ago, and Murphy's staying in Nikkō.{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikk%C5%8D,_Tochigi}

00:23:23.630 --> 00:23:24.940
Kyōto and...

00:23:24.940 --> 00:23:26.250
Nikkō, huh?

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:30.350
Yes. They're planned to be in
 the country for another eight days.

00:23:30.350 --> 00:23:32.260
And finally...

00:23:32.830 --> 00:23:39.140
Hitoshi Moriyama, 34. He is the ex-fiancé who was reponsible for the sister's suicide.

00:23:39.140 --> 00:23:46.440
Moriyama lived in Seattle, and worked at a trading company, but retired four years ago, and we don't know where he is now.

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:49.610
So two out of the three are in Japan...

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:52.110
He's going to target them for sure!

00:23:52.110 --> 00:23:57.380
Right. Alert the Kyōto and Tochigi Police immediately.

00:23:57.380 --> 00:24:02.550
Okay! Put out an urgent warrant looking for Timothy Hunter as a key person in this case!

00:24:02.550 --> 00:24:02.900
Right.

00:24:02.900 --> 00:24:03.580
Right!

00:24:04.600 --> 00:24:09.460
A former SEALs sniper... Looks like quite a shocking guy has turned up in Japan.

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:13.970
Yeah. And why did he have to choose Japan as the site of his revenge...

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:13.970
But at least I found out that <i>they</i> don't seem to be involved...

00:24:16.240 --> 00:24:22.560
Still, I wonder why that Hunter guy decided to seek revenge now, six years later?

00:24:22.560 --> 00:24:23.830
Right...

00:24:23.830 --> 00:24:25.710
I see what you mean.

00:24:25.780 --> 00:24:27.940
It just happened to be now, that's all.

00:24:27.940 --> 00:24:35.290
Still, you better stop playing your detective games! You almost died out there!

00:24:36.370 --> 00:24:37.320
And brat!

00:24:37.320 --> 00:24:40.010
You better not go wandering off either!

00:24:40.010 --> 00:24:40.830
Okay!

00:24:41.440 --> 00:24:42.840
Honestly...

00:24:42.840 --> 00:24:46.750
Sera-<i>san</i>, I am glad that you weren't hurt...

00:24:47.600 --> 00:24:49.500
But please don't put Conan-<i>kun</i>...

00:24:50.980 --> 00:24:53.760
Don't put Conan-<i>kun</i> in danger again, okay?

00:24:53.760 --> 00:24:54.930
Ran...

00:24:55.660 --> 00:24:59.850
Don't worry! I'll make sure to protect Conan-<i>kun</i>.

00:25:00.330 --> 00:25:05.100
Not to mention, there's no bullet that can shoot through Conan-<i>kun</i>'s heart right now.

00:25:05.100 --> 00:25:08.230
Or your heart either, of course!

00:25:08.230 --> 00:25:09.480
Huh?

00:25:09.480 --> 00:25:13.030
Bye! My bike's over this way.

00:25:13.030 --> 00:25:14.320
See you later, Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:25:14.320 --> 00:25:17.930
Unbelievable. Doesn't she realise what almost happened?

00:25:17.930 --> 00:25:21.630
I wonder why she said no bullet can shoot through my heart?

00:25:21.740 --> 00:25:25.460
Oh, maybe because you can flick them away with karate, Ran?

00:25:25.460 --> 00:25:27.710
Of course I can't!

00:25:28.060 --> 00:25:30.920
No, Ran might just be able to...

00:25:36.030 --> 00:25:40.630
What's wrong with you guys? I thought you'd be happier, with fireworks and all.

00:25:40.630 --> 00:25:43.770
Isn't it obvious? We watched someone being murdered!

00:25:43.770 --> 00:25:45.690
Well, I guess...

00:25:45.690 --> 00:25:47.120
And that's not all!

00:25:47.120 --> 00:25:47.520
Huh?

00:25:47.520 --> 00:25:50.520
They took all the photos we took!

00:25:50.520 --> 00:25:52.250
And all of our cameras!

00:25:52.250 --> 00:25:56.020
They're just holding onto them. They'll give them back soon.

00:25:56.020 --> 00:25:58.700
They might have something
 useful to the case, you never know.

00:26:00.120 --> 00:26:02.830
Oh, it went out... {wtf, shameless ayumi pantyshot}

00:26:03.470 --> 00:26:04.680
Oh, mine did too.

00:26:04.680 --> 00:26:05.660
Mine too.

00:26:12.550 --> 00:26:14.440
And that's the end of that.

00:26:14.440 --> 00:26:17.820
How about it, was that a nice diversion?

00:26:17.820 --> 00:26:19.420
It wasn't enough!

00:26:19.420 --> 00:26:21.020
It felt like something was missing...

00:26:21.020 --> 00:26:23.060
You should've bought some more fireworks!

00:26:24.460 --> 00:26:28.940
I thought you'd say that, so I got this ready!

00:26:31.860 --> 00:26:33.400
A Ball-Shooting Belt?

00:26:33.400 --> 00:26:36.650
This one's upgraded!

00:26:38.600 --> 00:26:41.240
Kick it as high as you can!

00:26:41.240 --> 00:26:43.740
I know, just hurry up and do it.

00:26:43.740 --> 00:26:47.070
Okay, let's set the timer...

00:26:47.070 --> 00:26:48.460
Here goes!

00:26:53.130 --> 00:26:55.090
Wow! It's really high!

00:26:55.090 --> 00:26:56.960
Okay! That'll do!

00:27:05.260 --> 00:27:08.270
Wow, that's great! Good work, doc!{uo, sugee! hakase yaru na!}

00:27:08.270 --> 00:27:09.600
It's wonderful!{o-migoto desu!}

00:27:09.600 --> 00:27:12.020
I call them Firework Balls!

00:27:12.020 --> 00:27:15.020
The neighbours are going to complain about this, you know?

00:27:15.020 --> 00:27:18.980
That might be a problem! What now, Ai-<i>kun</i>?!

00:27:19.180 --> 00:27:20.030
Geez...

00:27:20.030 --> 00:27:22.520
Must be great to be Conan-<i>kun</i>.

00:27:22.520 --> 00:27:23.890
You're so mean, doc!

00:27:23.890 --> 00:27:26.560
Don't you have anything for the rest of us?

00:27:27.170 --> 00:27:29.200
Well, you've got me there...

00:27:39.880 --> 00:27:41.180
Morning already?

00:27:42.110 --> 00:27:48.100
That Hitoshi Moriyama... I was sure I'd seen him in something like a newspaper article!

00:27:48.100 --> 00:27:50.940
Maybe I confused him with someone else.

00:27:51.460 --> 00:27:58.640
This is a list from FBI HQ, of the people Hunter is most likely to contact.

00:27:58.640 --> 00:27:59.640
Right...

00:27:59.640 --> 00:28:08.950
We've split into three teams to question them, but could you go over what the FBI knows about them once again?

00:28:08.950 --> 00:28:10.810
Of course.

00:28:10.810 --> 00:28:12.370
First, Scott Green.

00:28:13.150 --> 00:28:20.050
A former Navy chief petty officer who now runs a bicycle store in Machida to enjoy himself while earning money.

00:28:20.050 --> 00:28:26.200
When in the SEALs, he taught at the sniper school, and Hunter was one of his students.

00:28:26.200 --> 00:28:28.060
Next, Kevin Yoshino.

00:28:28.060 --> 00:28:34.270
A former Marine Corps staff sergeant who now runs a military shop in Fussa. {***}

00:28:34.270 --> 00:28:39.730
He uses his special connections to buy up former US military equipment for his shop.

00:28:40.210 --> 00:28:42.820
And finally, Mark Spencer.

00:28:43.340 --> 00:28:47.070
He wasn't on the list you read out yesterday.

00:28:47.070 --> 00:28:48.370
Right.

00:28:48.370 --> 00:28:57.750
Hunter has no direct connection to him, but he's an ex-admiral{shireikan***} who former US military soldiers in Japan often contact for advice.

00:28:57.750 --> 00:29:02.590
Since Hunter doesn't have a wide circle of friends, it's possible that he might be in contact with him.

00:29:02.590 --> 00:29:04.340
I see...

00:29:04.340 --> 00:29:11.720
He must've obtained his rifle and equipment from somewhere, so one of them might be helping him.

00:29:11.720 --> 00:29:12.520
Right.

00:29:13.500 --> 00:29:17.340
Tim— I mean, Hunter-<i>san</i>, wanted for sniping someone?!

00:29:17.340 --> 00:29:20.260
Well, we can't be completely sure yet...

00:29:20.260 --> 00:29:25.280
Apparently Hunter-<i>san</i> saved your life during the war in the Middle East?

00:29:25.280 --> 00:29:29.020
Yeah. I'd be dead if he hadn't been there.

00:29:29.020 --> 00:29:32.540
What if your rescuer came asking for your aid?

00:29:32.540 --> 00:29:39.290
For example, for an MK11, the gun used in the sniping?

00:29:39.290 --> 00:29:42.880
I don't even have one to give him!
 You think that's the real thing?

00:29:43.320 --> 00:29:46.380
You can buy it if you really want to check.

00:29:46.930 --> 00:29:48.640
You met Hunter?

00:29:48.640 --> 00:29:51.750
Yeah, he said he'd just arrived in Japan.

00:29:51.750 --> 00:29:53.020
Where is he now?

00:29:53.020 --> 00:29:56.350
Sorry, but I wouldn't know.

00:29:56.350 --> 00:29:59.480
The sniper fled by bike.

00:29:59.480 --> 00:30:02.360
It was a recently repaired second-hand bike with a fake number plate.

00:30:02.360 --> 00:30:05.110
You trying to say I helped him?

00:30:05.110 --> 00:30:08.860
Sorry to disappoint you, but I only sell <i>new</i> bikes.

00:30:09.710 --> 00:30:13.490
How do you feel about Hunter-<i>san</i>'s violation of the Rules of Engagement?

00:30:15.410 --> 00:30:16.750
I can't reject the facts.

00:30:17.890 --> 00:30:25.720
Overeager to protect his comrades, he misjudged and shot a defenceless civilian.

00:30:26.260 --> 00:30:31.550
You're wrong! Hunter-<i>san</i> would never have done that! He was framed!

00:30:31.550 --> 00:30:33.600
Framed?

00:30:34.140 --> 00:30:38.390
That Waltz guy was jealous of Hunter-<i>san</i>, his replacement.

00:30:38.860 --> 00:30:41.270
So Jack Waltz was a sniper too?

00:30:41.270 --> 00:30:45.420
So he stole away Hunter-<i>san</i>'s Silver Star...

00:30:46.400 --> 00:30:48.190
…and even... {ORDERED FOR HIM TO BE SHOT! ...but that would be a spoiler}

00:30:49.910 --> 00:30:53.290
You think there was no violation, then?

00:30:53.290 --> 00:30:55.580
Yeah, of course.

00:30:55.580 --> 00:31:00.790
Hunter-<i>san</i> was a hero, he saved the lives of lots of soldiers out there...

00:31:01.420 --> 00:31:04.010
And if he <i>did</i> come and ask for my help...

00:31:04.010 --> 00:31:06.300
I'd gladly help him.

00:31:07.340 --> 00:31:08.800
I wouldn't know.

00:31:08.800 --> 00:31:14.140
I've never met Hunter, and
 haven't heard anything about him.

00:31:14.140 --> 00:31:16.000
Is that right...

00:31:16.000 --> 00:31:21.050
Then how do you feel about Hunter-<i>san</i>'s violation of the Rules of Engagement?

00:31:21.050 --> 00:31:24.060
It doesn't matter whether it happened or not.

00:31:24.060 --> 00:31:31.450
If Hunter was behind this sniping, then I can never forgive him, on my pride as a fellow former Marine.

00:31:32.600 --> 00:31:34.830
Shoot him dead the moment you find him.

00:31:34.830 --> 00:31:37.080
S-Shoot him...?

00:31:37.680 --> 00:31:44.920
Your police snipers don't have a hope of beating him. Why don't I lend you my chauffeur?

00:31:44.920 --> 00:31:46.380
Carlos!

00:31:46.380 --> 00:31:47.040
Sir.

00:31:48.210 --> 00:31:56.220
Carlos Lee. A former Marine sniper.
 He picked up 36 kills in the Middle East.

00:31:56.220 --> 00:32:00.730
That's just counting confirmed kills. If you include the unconfirmed ones, it's 78 kills in all.

00:32:00.730 --> 00:32:02.980
Oh, right.

00:32:02.980 --> 00:32:07.480
Well, even so, it doesn't match up to Hunter's 79 kills.

00:32:08.090 --> 00:32:11.490
But only a sniper can beat a sniper.

00:32:11.490 --> 00:32:14.150
So how about it, do you want him?

00:32:25.230 --> 00:32:28.840
If he wasn't in any of the newspapers, then he must've been in a girls' magazine.

00:32:28.840 --> 00:32:32.260
But this is going to be a big job...

00:32:32.260 --> 00:32:34.980
Okay, let's spread out the map on the table.

00:32:34.980 --> 00:32:36.260
Right!

00:32:36.260 --> 00:32:38.970
First, we should decide how
 big a range we want to include.

00:32:38.970 --> 00:32:42.350
Oh, I see you're jumping straight into your homework!

00:32:42.350 --> 00:32:43.560
Of course!

00:32:43.560 --> 00:32:48.070
That's wonderful! And wonderful kids deserve a reward.

00:32:48.070 --> 00:32:49.580
What is it? What is it?

00:32:49.580 --> 00:32:51.820
You're giving us Firework Belts too?!

00:32:51.820 --> 00:32:58.240
Well, no, they'll annoy the neighbours.
 So I've got something more practical for you.

00:32:58.240 --> 00:33:00.550
Huh? Detective Badges?

00:33:00.550 --> 00:33:01.750
They've been upgraded.

00:33:01.750 --> 00:33:05.820
I made some improvements, and now they've got better reception.

00:33:05.820 --> 00:33:09.470
It seems <i>someone</i> called them ‘pieces of junk’, and really hurt his feelings.

00:33:09.470 --> 00:33:11.510
What, you could hear that?

00:33:12.450 --> 00:33:14.510
They look the same as before...

00:33:14.510 --> 00:33:17.450
The reception's the only change?

00:33:17.450 --> 00:33:19.210
That's so boring...

00:33:19.760 --> 00:33:21.500
That's not all that's different!

00:33:21.500 --> 00:33:24.980
If you change the setting, and then press the button to talk...

00:33:24.980 --> 00:33:26.960
Ah! They lit up!

00:33:26.960 --> 00:33:28.730
LED lamps, right?

00:33:28.730 --> 00:33:30.630
Wow, they're cooler than before!

00:33:30.630 --> 00:33:31.300
Yeah!

00:33:31.300 --> 00:33:33.610
You can even choose the colour,
 and which badges to light up!

00:33:33.610 --> 00:33:35.140
Wow! That's great!

00:33:35.140 --> 00:33:38.300
But they're making a weird noise, aren't they?

00:33:38.620 --> 00:33:40.150
Huh?!

00:33:40.150 --> 00:33:41.490
Ah!

00:33:41.490 --> 00:33:43.220
I can't hear a thing...

00:33:43.220 --> 00:33:45.740
What? You can't hear it, doc?

00:33:45.740 --> 00:33:47.420
That's mosquito noise.

00:33:47.420 --> 00:33:53.300
High-frequency noises get harder to hear when you get older, so adults can't hear it.

00:33:53.300 --> 00:33:57.130
I guess it must be an accidental side-effect of the improvements I made...

00:33:57.130 --> 00:33:59.260
I'll fix them later.

00:33:59.260 --> 00:34:04.410
Aren't they're fine like this? Who knows, the mosquito noise might come in handy.

00:34:04.410 --> 00:34:08.470
But I guess this means they're faulty...

00:34:08.470 --> 00:34:10.230
That's so lame!

00:34:10.230 --> 00:34:13.280
And I was just getting excited about them...

00:34:13.460 --> 00:34:16.760
All right! Then how about an exciting quiz!

00:34:16.760 --> 00:34:18.050
What?

00:34:18.050 --> 00:34:19.150
Another one?

00:34:19.150 --> 00:34:20.620
It'll just be another pun...

00:34:21.240 --> 00:34:23.540
It won't hurt to hear him out, right?

00:34:23.540 --> 00:34:25.460
R-Right! 

00:34:23.540 --> 00:34:25.680
Well, if you say so, Ai-<i>chan</i>...

00:34:25.680 --> 00:34:27.020
Only for you, Haibara-<i>san</i>...

00:34:27.020 --> 00:34:28.290
Oh well...

00:34:28.290 --> 00:34:30.290
All right! Then here goes!

00:34:30.290 --> 00:34:38.300
A sniper looking for vinegar challenges you to rock-paper-scissors. What should you play to beat him?

00:34:38.300 --> 00:34:41.620
The English word ‘sniper’ is a hint!{sniper}

00:34:41.620 --> 00:34:43.350
What's a sniper?

00:34:43.350 --> 00:34:44.700
English, huh...?

00:34:44.700 --> 00:34:46.280
Did you work it out, Conan-<i>kun</i>?

00:34:46.280 --> 00:34:50.520
Y-Yeah. But you won't like the answer.

00:34:50.520 --> 00:34:52.690
I don't know English!

00:34:52.690 --> 00:34:53.400
We give up.

00:34:53.400 --> 00:34:55.070
What's the answer?!

00:34:55.070 --> 00:34:57.220
The answer is scissors!

00:34:57.220 --> 00:35:05.020
su nai kaa?

00:34:57.220 --> 00:35:05.020
sunaipaa

00:34:57.220 --> 00:35:05.020
You're up against a sniper{sunaipaa}, who's asking ‘Got any vinegar?{su nai kaa?}’, so scissors would beat him in rock-paper-scissors!

00:35:05.020 --> 00:35:06.890
‘Got any vinegar’?!

00:35:06.890 --> 00:35:08.740
So it's ‘kaa’ and ‘paa’?

00:35:08.740 --> 00:35:12.080
paa

00:35:08.740 --> 00:35:12.080
And so you're saying scissors would win because he'd pick paper{paa}?

00:35:13.130 --> 00:35:14.840
‘Got any vinegar’?

00:35:14.840 --> 00:35:16.780
Well, since he's a sni—

00:35:16.780 --> 00:35:17.600
Ahem.

00:35:17.600 --> 00:35:18.090
Huh?

00:35:19.460 --> 00:35:23.350
Which of these three sports are snipers best at?

00:35:23.350 --> 00:35:24.810
1. Baseball.

00:35:24.810 --> 00:35:26.700
2. Football.

00:35:26.700 --> 00:35:28.310
3. Golf.

00:35:29.530 --> 00:35:31.610
W-Well, it's...

00:35:31.610 --> 00:35:33.400
The answer is number three.

00:35:33.400 --> 00:35:37.740
naisu paa

00:35:33.400 --> 00:35:37.740
sunaipaa

00:35:33.400 --> 00:35:37.740
If you rearrange the word ‘sniper{sunaipaa}’, it makes ‘nice par{naisu paa}’.{Nice par is wasei-eigo for Good par}

00:35:34.360 --> 00:35:37.190
SUNAIPAA

00:35:35.900 --> 00:35:37.190
NAISU PAA

00:35:37.740 --> 00:35:39.210
Amazing, Ai-<i>chan</i>!

00:35:39.210 --> 00:35:40.630
That was great, Haibara-<i>san</i>!

00:35:40.630 --> 00:35:41.700
Nice par?

00:35:41.700 --> 00:35:44.070
I guess Haibara can do the quizzes from now on.

00:35:44.070 --> 00:35:47.880
T-Then all my clever wordplay counts for nothing?!

00:35:47.880 --> 00:35:51.360
Hey, let's forget about him and go do our homework!

00:35:51.360 --> 00:35:52.210
Right.

00:35:52.210 --> 00:35:53.990
Let's do it!

00:35:54.660 --> 00:35:56.090
I should've done my homework…{kyoushuku dai... *** recheck animanga/BD}

00:35:56.570 --> 00:36:02.230
Oh, you lost your phone, right?
 Apparently the police were in contact about it.

00:36:02.230 --> 00:36:04.600
Oh, doc...

00:36:04.600 --> 00:36:07.250
Surely <i>that's</i> more important than a quiz.

00:36:07.250 --> 00:36:09.600
Also, about Masumi Sera...

00:36:10.480 --> 00:36:13.480
Be careful. She's dangerous.

00:36:14.860 --> 00:36:17.040
You're one to talk.

00:36:18.360 --> 00:36:20.380
Huh? Conan-<i>kun</i>?

00:36:20.380 --> 00:36:20.930
Huh?

00:36:20.930 --> 00:36:22.930
He's going to pick up his lost phone.

00:36:22.930 --> 00:36:25.120
Let's start without him.

00:36:27.620 --> 00:36:34.500
Thank you for your patronage. Beika Library is about to close. Please return any books you are reading to their shelves.{***check animanga/BD for v2}


00:36:32.980 --> 00:36:36.840
How weird... Maybe I really did
 confuse him for someone else.

00:36:36.840 --> 00:36:39.170
Oh! Bingo!

00:36:39.170 --> 00:36:43.180
‘Hitoshi and Nami Yasuhara’

00:36:39.170 --> 00:36:41.260
Hitoshi Yasuhara.

00:36:41.260 --> 00:36:43.180
Huh? Not Moriyama?

00:36:43.180 --> 00:36:46.970
He started a private import service four years ago...

00:36:46.970 --> 00:36:52.070
His wife is a charismatic cooking expert. 
She runs cookery classes in Honjo, Sumida City...

00:36:52.070 --> 00:36:54.070
Excuse me... We're about to close.

00:36:54.070 --> 00:36:57.070
Oh, right. I'll tidy up in just a moment.

00:36:57.070 --> 00:36:58.610
{missing} Sorry for the trouble.

00:36:58.610 --> 00:37:03.400
‘Hitoshi Yasuhara-<i>san</i> chose to take his wife, Nami-<i>san</i>'s surname when getting married.’

00:37:03.400 --> 00:37:07.410
I get it! His name changed
 because he took his wife's name!

00:37:07.980 --> 00:37:12.910
We should be chasing after that Organisation, but now we've ended up involved in this tough case...

00:37:12.910 --> 00:37:14.300
Yes.

00:37:14.460 --> 00:37:18.790
Still, we're outclassed. To think we're facing a former SEALs sniper...

00:37:19.870 --> 00:37:23.050
If only Akai-<i>san</i> was here...

00:37:23.050 --> 00:37:25.020
I'm sorry...

00:37:25.020 --> 00:37:28.800
It's fine. I was thinking the same thing.

00:37:30.190 --> 00:37:39.620
Shū, there's something I'd like to ask. Who has the best sniping technique — police shooters or military snipers?

00:37:39.620 --> 00:37:41.460
It depends on the conditions.

00:37:41.460 --> 00:37:42.630
Huh?

00:37:42.910 --> 00:37:51.590
If the range is less than 100 metres, then police shooters. They are trained to be more precise with their shots.

00:37:51.590 --> 00:37:52.200
Really?

00:37:52.200 --> 00:37:53.690
Yeah...

00:37:53.790 --> 00:37:57.710
Police shooters are usually called in when hostages are involved.

00:37:58.290 --> 00:38:05.720
They need to have extremely accurate aim, to be able to stop the target from moving in an instant.

00:38:05.720 --> 00:38:13.750
There's only one spot where you can kill someone with a single bullet, and cut off all possible convulsions.

00:38:13.750 --> 00:38:14.980
The brain stem...

00:38:14.980 --> 00:38:16.940
Right.

00:38:16.940 --> 00:38:21.320
If you hit anywhere else, for example, even if you shoot through their heart,

00:38:21.320 --> 00:38:24.570
targets can keep fighting for anywhere up to ten seconds.

00:38:24.570 --> 00:38:29.740
And so there's the danger that they'll take their hostages, and even other police officers with them to the grave.

00:38:29.740 --> 00:38:31.580
But where should you aim?

00:38:32.090 --> 00:38:40.500
Face the target head on, and aim for the tip of their nose. How about it, think you can do it?

00:38:42.110 --> 00:38:48.430
Don't worry. As long as I'm around, you'll never have to do something like that.

00:38:49.700 --> 00:38:51.400
I promise.

00:38:58.890 --> 00:39:00.190
Shū...

00:39:07.190 --> 00:39:09.440
Thank you!

00:39:09.440 --> 00:39:11.890
Be careful not to lose it again, okay?

00:39:11.890 --> 00:39:13.270
Right!

00:39:16.300 --> 00:39:18.830
Conan-<i>kun</i>?! What have you been doing?!

00:39:18.830 --> 00:39:20.460
Oh, I lost my phone.

00:39:20.460 --> 00:39:23.020
So that's why you weren't answering...

00:39:23.020 --> 00:39:26.060
Sorry. But did something happen?

00:39:26.060 --> 00:39:29.470
Yeah. I found who I think is Hitoshi Moriyama.

00:39:29.470 --> 00:39:32.670
I'm about to go and meet him to find ou—{out}

00:39:32.670 --> 00:39:34.220
Wait! I'll come too!

00:39:34.220 --> 00:39:35.860
But where are you right now?

00:39:35.860 --> 00:39:38.740
Outside the Azuma Bridge Police Box in Honjo, Sumida City.

00:39:38.740 --> 00:39:42.060
That's a surprise. I'm in Honjo too.

00:39:42.060 --> 00:39:43.240
What? Really?

00:39:43.240 --> 00:39:43.900
Yeah.

00:39:43.900 --> 00:39:48.900
It seems fate wants us to solve this case.

00:40:18.140 --> 00:40:21.190
Yeah. Just turn left.

00:40:21.310 --> 00:40:22.560
You got here quick, Conan-<i>kun</i>.

00:40:22.560 --> 00:40:25.260
Yeah. Have you spotted any signs of movement?

00:40:25.260 --> 00:40:27.470
Don't worry, nothing yet.

00:40:27.580 --> 00:40:29.610
Okay, ready to go in?

00:40:29.610 --> 00:40:30.900
Yeah.

00:40:32.110 --> 00:40:35.120
A vehicle is about to leave. Please be careful.

00:40:33.640 --> 00:40:35.120
Oh, no!

00:41:07.430 --> 00:41:10.290
Oh, crap! Run, Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:41:14.900 --> 00:41:16.160
N-No...

00:41:36.260 --> 00:41:40.140
There's two places that shot could've come from. Which do you think it was?

00:41:40.140 --> 00:41:42.680
I bet it was the higher one. What do you think?

00:41:42.680 --> 00:41:45.690
Yeah. I was thinking it was the taller one too.

00:41:46.590 --> 00:41:50.610
If you connect the bullet holes in the windscreen and Moriyama-<i>san</i> with a straight line,

00:41:50.610 --> 00:41:53.620
the closer, shorter building looks
 like it was the sniping position...

00:41:53.620 --> 00:41:57.990
But Moriyama-<i>san</i>'s car was still halfway in his underground garage when he was shot.

00:41:57.990 --> 00:42:04.750
Which means you have to add in the angle of the slope to calculate the real angle of the shot.

00:42:04.960 --> 00:42:09.330
And there's only one tall building in line with the shot!

00:42:11.250 --> 00:42:13.260
This is it, right?

00:42:13.260 --> 00:42:16.260
Wait, Conan-<i>kun</i>! You can't just go in there alone!

00:42:16.260 --> 00:42:18.110
Damn!

00:42:23.300 --> 00:42:26.680
Excuse me! You need to be signed in!{adapted, literally 'Can I please ask for you to listen to me?' ***recheck animanga/BD}

00:42:26.860 --> 00:42:29.100
Damn, he's so reckless!

00:42:29.100 --> 00:42:32.980
And Hunter could still be here too!

00:42:49.290 --> 00:42:51.340
A three? Don't tell me...

00:42:51.340 --> 00:42:52.290
Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:42:52.290 --> 00:42:55.350
Hey, look at this...

00:42:56.260 --> 00:42:58.520
Then he really <i>did</i> snipe from here...

00:42:58.520 --> 00:42:59.570
Yeah.

00:43:06.930 --> 00:43:10.440
‘Police HQ’

00:43:06.930 --> 00:43:10.440
So Moriyama-<i>san</i> was back in Japan too...

00:43:10.440 --> 00:43:12.710
Yes. We were careless...

00:43:12.710 --> 00:43:18.840
With these two being murdered, I think we can conclude that Hunter is the sniper for sure.

00:43:18.840 --> 00:43:23.700
Right. The bullets were even 7.62 mm calibre, matching Hunter's favourite gun, the MK11.

00:43:23.700 --> 00:43:29.580
Also, the scenes of the snipings themselves tell us that Hunter was behind them.

00:43:29.580 --> 00:43:30.700
What do you mean?

00:43:30.700 --> 00:43:32.760
Akahoshi-<i>kun</i>, if you would explain...

00:43:32.760 --> 00:43:33.890
Right.

00:43:34.520 --> 00:43:41.340
Fujinami-<i>san</i> always invited his marks out to visit high places, to make their property viewings into a deluxe show.

00:43:42.100 --> 00:43:45.850
He probably tricked Hunter in the same way.

00:43:45.850 --> 00:43:51.270
You mean that's why he chose to snipe Fujinami-<i>san</i> during a property viewing?

00:43:51.270 --> 00:43:52.900
Yes.

00:43:52.900 --> 00:43:58.190
According to an estate agent he worked with, Fujinami-<i>san</i> bought up lots of pre-opening tickets to the Bell Tree Tower

00:43:58.190 --> 00:44:04.370
through a backroom deal, and was showing off properties from that spot almost every day.

00:44:04.570 --> 00:44:11.710
And Moriyama-<i>san</i> broke off his engagement with Hunter's sister, and married another woman.

00:44:11.710 --> 00:44:17.300
That's probably why he picked the home of his love to be his murder scene.

00:44:17.340 --> 00:44:23.800
Moriyama-<i>san</i> went to meet his wife at her cookery classes at the same time every day.

00:44:23.800 --> 00:44:25.890
 We believe that's what Hunter was aiming for.

00:44:25.890 --> 00:44:32.980
But on the days of both snipings, doors and cameras had been shot through with a gun to let him through.

00:44:32.980 --> 00:44:35.870
He must've visited again and again to check beforehand and gather information.

00:44:35.870 --> 00:44:41.950
His snipings were carefully thought-out and meticulously planned — exactly what you'd expect from a SEALs sniper.

00:44:41.950 --> 00:44:43.100
Yes.

00:44:43.350 --> 00:44:48.410
Speaking of careful plans, did he leave a shell and a die at this sniping too?

00:44:48.410 --> 00:44:53.330
Oh, yes. Right at the sniping position. Here's a photo.

00:44:53.790 --> 00:44:56.390
This time, the die shows a three...?

00:44:56.390 --> 00:44:58.590
Last time it was a four, wasn't it?

00:44:58.590 --> 00:45:02.420
Could this be... a countdown?

00:45:04.100 --> 00:45:05.010
I see...

00:45:05.010 --> 00:45:11.020
That means Hunter has four targets in Japan in total.

00:45:11.720 --> 00:45:16.520
He killed Hiroaki Fujinami-<i>san</i>
 and Hitoshi Moriyama-<i>san</i> already,

00:45:16.520 --> 00:45:24.700
and is planning to murder two more people, leaving dice showing the numbers two and one where he snipes them.

00:45:24.700 --> 00:45:26.540
This is terrible...

00:45:26.540 --> 00:45:29.950
If this theory's right, then the other two victims will be...

00:45:29.950 --> 00:45:35.800
Yes. He's sure to go after Jack Waltz-<i>san</i> and Bill Murphy-<i>san</i>.

00:45:35.800 --> 00:45:36.960
Speaking of those two...

00:45:36.960 --> 00:45:43.970
The local police forces have told each of them about the snipings, and they've changed their sightseeing schedules.

00:45:43.970 --> 00:45:50.440
Originally, they intended to meet in Tōkyō in two days,

00:45:50.440 --> 00:45:54.730
but now they've both decided to stay in their hotels until the case is dealt with.

00:45:54.730 --> 00:46:00.070
Waltz-<i>san</i>'s family wanted to head straight back to America immediately,

00:46:00.070 --> 00:46:08.740
but there's a chance that Hunter may have anticipated and planned for that, so they're stuck at their hotel for now.

00:46:08.740 --> 00:46:11.840
That may be the best choice...

00:46:11.840 --> 00:46:12.870
Right...

00:46:12.870 --> 00:46:17.290
With the local police on alert, he won't be able to get to them easily,

00:46:17.850 --> 00:46:24.300
and with strict checks set up around Kyōto and Nikkō,
 it won't be easy for Hunter to enter either city anymore.

00:46:24.300 --> 00:46:27.550
Still, that doesn't give us leave to sit idly by.

00:46:28.080 --> 00:46:33.990
It's likely that Hunter is still in Tōkyō! We have to find him, no matter what!

00:46:33.990 --> 00:46:35.310
Right!

00:47:39.040 --> 00:47:41.730
What is it, Conan-<i>kun</i>?

00:47:42.230 --> 00:47:44.350
Yeah. Right...

00:47:44.350 --> 00:47:47.260
What?! Hunter was shot dead?!

00:47:47.260 --> 00:47:52.260
They still haven't confirmed his identity, but I doubt it could be anyone else.

00:47:47.260 --> 00:47:52.260
Early this morning, an American man was shot dead in an abandoned building in Azuma Bridge first district{***CHECK HANDLING BEFORE RELEASE!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!}, Sumida City, Tōkyō.

00:47:52.260 --> 00:47:57.020
Right. I'll let you know when I know more.

00:47:52.260 --> 00:47:57.020
He is believed to be Timothy Hunter.  

00:47:57.480 --> 00:48:05.710
We found a diary in Hunter's hideout, and after translating it, we were shocked by what he had written.

00:48:05.710 --> 00:48:07.530
Here's a photo of it.

00:48:07.530 --> 00:48:12.030
‘August 3rd. He is challenging me, stealing my prey again.’

00:48:12.030 --> 00:48:15.290
‘He obviously wants a piece of me.’

00:48:15.290 --> 00:48:20.990
‘I have to find a way to kill him {in}and get the last two targets myself.’

00:48:21.100 --> 00:48:27.920
From this, we can understand that someone else killed Fujinami-<i>san</i> and Moriyama-<i>san</i> before Hunter had a chance to.

00:48:27.920 --> 00:48:33.930
Then, the real sniper challenged Hunter to a direct contest, and won...

00:48:34.530 --> 00:48:39.360
If so, then that means the man
 we saw wasn't Hunter either...

00:48:39.360 --> 00:48:45.190
We believe his sniper shot from a floating platform in Sumida River facing the hideout,

00:48:45.190 --> 00:48:50.230
and found a shell and a die showing the number two there.

00:48:51.420 --> 00:48:53.740
One thing was different this time.

00:48:53.740 --> 00:48:58.990
Despite having the closest range of any of the snipings at only 150 metres,

00:48:58.990 --> 00:49:03.930
there was a bullet embedded into Hunter's door which we believe to be a missed shot.

00:49:03.930 --> 00:49:07.710
There was also a bullet mark on the floating platform which we think was a missed shot,

00:49:07.710 --> 00:49:10.730
and forensics are searching the area for anything else.

00:49:10.730 --> 00:49:15.320
We told the media not to mention 
the shells and the dice, right?

00:49:16.030 --> 00:49:26.350
And so to find them at this sniping position means that all three snipings, including Hunter's, were likely by the same man.

00:49:26.350 --> 00:49:32.360
And there was no shell or die at the first sniping position in Seattle to begin with...

00:49:32.360 --> 00:49:37.300
Perhaps Hunter was responsible only for the sniping of Mr Brian Woods?

00:49:37.300 --> 00:49:40.870
Right. That would explain it.

00:49:40.870 --> 00:49:46.920
And if that explanation is right, we need to pay attention to the numbers on the dice.

00:49:46.920 --> 00:49:51.750
Four, three, two, and then... Next would be one?

00:49:51.750 --> 00:49:53.300
Then there's going to be another sniping?!

00:49:53.300 --> 00:49:57.500
Yes. But we have no way to stop it.

00:49:57.500 --> 00:49:58.550
I see...

00:49:58.550 --> 00:50:07.940
The reasons we expected Jack Waltz-<i>san</i> and Bill Murphy-<i>san</i> to be targeted no longer apply.

00:50:07.940 --> 00:50:14.400
Yes. And now we have absolutely no idea who will be the next target.

00:50:14.860 --> 00:50:17.420
The worst possible development...

00:50:21.030 --> 00:50:28.430
Early this morning, a third sniping occurred in an abandoned building in Azuma Bridge first district{***CHECK HANDLING BEFORE RELEASE!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!}, Sumida City, Tōkyō.

00:50:28.430 --> 00:50:33.420
The victim is thought to be Timothy Hunter-<i>san</i>, 37,

00:50:33.420 --> 00:50:41.550
an American and former US SEALs sniper who the police believed to be behind the recent sniping spree.

00:50:35.550 --> 00:50:41.550
Timothy Hunter-<i>san</i> (37) — Former US Navy SEAL

00:50:41.550 --> 00:50:50.520
The police haven't given out any details yet, but shouldn't we consider this sniping to be by the same sniper as the last two?

00:50:50.520 --> 00:50:56.940
<i>A  sniping spree... What's next?!</i>

00:50:50.520 --> 00:50:52.330
Huh? But that means...

00:50:52.330 --> 00:50:56.940
That this won't be the end of the sniping spree.
 And we don't know who'll be the sniper's next target.

00:50:57.790 --> 00:51:00.300
What?! Then it's an utterly random killing spree?!

00:51:00.300 --> 00:51:07.420
Oh, I wouldn't go quite that far. But if they don't catch the sniper soon, people will be scared to go outside.

00:51:05.070 --> 00:51:07.930
Did you hear? It's a random killing spree! Scary! 

00:51:07.930 --> 00:51:10.700
There's tons of helicopters flying around Sumida River!

00:51:10.700 --> 00:51:12.550
Is it dangerous to be in Shitamachi?!

00:51:12.550 --> 00:51:15.000
No, I heard Shibuya was next.

00:51:15.000 --> 00:51:17.170
Really?! I better take the underground...

00:51:17.870 --> 00:51:20.660
That's right, I heard Harajuku's dangerous!

00:51:20.660 --> 00:51:24.180
It's all fake, don't let this rubbish fool you! Idiots!

00:51:24.180 --> 00:51:26.890
Not a soul in Takeshita Street! What a sight!

00:51:26.890 --> 00:51:28.180
There's never been anything like this before, has there?

00:51:28.180 --> 00:51:32.190
Asakusa's gotta be the key. Apparently children are banned from going outside there.

00:51:32.190 --> 00:51:36.190
You an idiot? All the previous victims were adults!

00:51:36.190 --> 00:51:40.700
There ain't even any old folks visiting the temples... What's going on?

00:51:40.700 --> 00:51:44.700
The Bell Tree Tower was where the first one took place, and it's still being repaired, right?

00:51:44.700 --> 00:51:49.630
By the way, apparently you could see the Bell Tree from where the other snipings happened!

00:51:49.630 --> 00:51:51.480
You could see the Bell Tree, that's right!

00:51:51.480 --> 00:51:53.210
Does that mean the Bell Tree's the key to this case?!

00:51:53.910 --> 00:51:57.210
That means it doesn't matter how far you are, if you can still see the Bell Tree!

00:51:57.210 --> 00:52:01.220
Umbrellas! You can't be seen from above with an umbrella, so you'll be safe!

00:52:12.790 --> 00:52:14.730
That was awesome!{chou ukeru!}

00:52:18.150 --> 00:52:23.000
In all, five people were wounded, several with severe injuries. And that ends our report from the scene at Kinshi Town.


00:52:23.330 --> 00:52:26.330
Looks like all of Tōkyō's in a panic...

00:52:26.330 --> 00:52:30.890
Word of an ‘utterly random killing spree’ spreads quickly...

00:52:30.890 --> 00:52:36.710
Well, it's no surprise. This is the first time there's ever been a sniping spree in Japan.

00:52:36.710 --> 00:52:37.340
Here.

00:52:37.340 --> 00:52:39.370
Thanks, Ran-<i>chan</i>.

00:52:39.370 --> 00:52:40.700
Thanks for the tea.

00:52:40.700 --> 00:52:43.970
So, any idea who the sniper is?

00:52:45.180 --> 00:52:46.350
Well...

00:52:46.350 --> 00:52:51.400
To be honest, Hunter's death
 threw our investigation into chaos.

00:52:51.400 --> 00:52:55.760
So we came to ask if you had any ideas, Mouri-<i>san</i>...

00:52:55.760 --> 00:52:57.270
I see...

00:52:57.270 --> 00:53:00.990
Come on, asking that old man ain't gonna help you...

00:52:59.750 --> 00:53:00.990
Well, let's see...  

00:53:00.990 --> 00:53:07.240
First, we can be sure that the sniper was connected with Hunter somehow.

00:53:07.240 --> 00:53:08.410
Right.

00:53:08.410 --> 00:53:13.250
And the only people in Japan that
 knew Hunter were Scott Green,

00:53:13.250 --> 00:53:17.300
his former teacher at sniping school, and originally a SEALs sniper himself...

00:53:17.300 --> 00:53:20.500
...and the ex-Marine, Kevin Yoshino.

00:53:20.500 --> 00:53:24.410
To tell you the truth, both of them vanished last night...

00:53:24.410 --> 00:53:25.460
What?

00:53:25.460 --> 00:53:29.680
But neither of them had a motive for murdering Hunter.

00:53:29.680 --> 00:53:32.310
Then what about his murder...?

00:53:32.310 --> 00:53:37.030
We suspect it's a third party who we haven't found yet.

00:53:37.030 --> 00:53:41.320
No, there's one person you're forgetting!

00:53:41.320 --> 00:53:46.700
The former admiral of Yokosuka Base, the retired Rear Admiral, Mark Spencer...

00:53:47.290 --> 00:53:48.010
But—

00:53:48.010 --> 00:53:54.120
His chauffeur. The ex-Marine sniper, Carlos Lee!

00:53:54.690 --> 00:53:58.220
But neither Spencer-<i>san</i> nor Lee-<i>san</i>
 are connected with Hunter...

00:53:58.220 --> 00:54:00.040
Right! To begin with, what motive would he have?

00:54:00.040 --> 00:54:03.070
His motive is his pride as a sniper!

00:54:03.070 --> 00:54:04.090
Pride?

00:54:04.090 --> 00:54:04.550
Yeah.

00:54:04.550 --> 00:54:09.320
Hunter managed 79 kills on the front line. How about Lee?

00:54:09.320 --> 00:54:14.350
U-Uhh... 36 kills in the Middle East.

00:54:14.350 --> 00:54:18.100
That's just the confirmed ones.
 If you add in the unconfirmed ones...

00:54:18.100 --> 00:54:19.270
U-Uhh, right...

00:54:19.820 --> 00:54:22.260
I think it was 78 kills.

00:54:22.260 --> 00:54:23.280
Right!

00:54:23.280 --> 00:54:34.660
And Lee couldn't bear it. He thought his skills as a sniper were the best. Then, he heard Hunter killed Woods in Seattle.

00:54:34.660 --> 00:54:40.630
Hunter got his 80th kill. So Lee decided to anticipate his next move...

00:54:41.630 --> 00:54:44.460
And killed Fujinami-<i>san</i> and Moriyama-<i>san</i>!

00:54:44.460 --> 00:54:53.890
That makes it 80 versus 80. Lee finally managed to catch up with Hunter, so he decided to challenge Hunter to a final contest.

00:54:54.670 --> 00:54:55.700
Bang!

00:54:55.700 --> 00:54:59.310
Got it! We'll look into it!

00:54:59.310 --> 00:55:01.230
R-Right...

00:55:01.230 --> 00:55:02.790
Thank you so much!

00:55:02.790 --> 00:55:04.620
Thank you!

00:55:06.560 --> 00:55:09.780
That was amazing, Dad!

00:55:12.840 --> 00:55:16.200
It was an odd deduction, but it makes sense.

00:55:16.200 --> 00:55:20.920
Well, whether the old man's theory is right or not, I need more information.

00:55:22.220 --> 00:55:23.920
New information, huh...

00:55:24.560 --> 00:55:31.770
That's right, the size of the bullet retrieved from Hunter's corpse was 5.56 × 45 mm.

00:55:31.770 --> 00:55:35.430
It's lighter than the previous bullets, and didn't go all the way through his head.

00:55:35.430 --> 00:55:38.040
Huh? It was a different type of bullet?

00:55:38.040 --> 00:55:45.440
Yes. The wounds on the corpse were so light that despite having been shot in the head, we immediately knew it was Hunter.

00:55:45.440 --> 00:55:49.340
He used another gun's bullets because of the closer range?

00:55:49.340 --> 00:55:54.000
Right. They'd have less recoil, and be more accurate.

00:55:54.220 --> 00:55:55.870
And yet he missed a shot...

00:55:56.820 --> 00:55:58.580
That is strange...

00:55:58.580 --> 00:56:00.620
Have you found out anything else?

00:56:00.620 --> 00:56:02.710
There is one thing that bugged me.

00:56:02.710 --> 00:56:07.710
When I saw Hunter's body at the university hospital, he seemed to have lost a lot of weight.

00:56:07.880 --> 00:56:09.220
He lost weight?

00:56:09.220 --> 00:56:13.470
Yes. He looked like a different man to when he was awarded the Silver Star...

00:56:14.560 --> 00:56:20.100
I think you better do a clinical autopsy as well as the forensic autopsy.

00:56:21.370 --> 00:56:23.740
Also, do an X-ray of his skull.

00:56:23.740 --> 00:56:26.150
Got it. I'll go and talk to Inspector Megure.

00:56:26.320 --> 00:56:28.280
Okay, I'll talk to you later.

00:56:29.330 --> 00:56:31.030
Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:56:31.030 --> 00:56:34.520
Where are you going? It's dangerous
 outside, so don't go too far.

00:56:34.520 --> 00:56:38.740
Sure, don't worry. I'm just going to get my skateboard back from Dr. Agasa.

00:56:38.740 --> 00:56:41.620
Oh, wait, Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:56:47.980 --> 00:56:52.650
Yeah, I heard. But who'd want to kill Hunter?

00:56:52.650 --> 00:56:54.680
Yeah, I have no idea...

00:56:54.680 --> 00:56:59.220
Well, at least I don't have to worry about Hunter coming after me anymore.

00:56:59.220 --> 00:57:02.230
Remind me to thank his killer...

00:57:02.230 --> 00:57:06.190
Right. But we still better be careful.

00:57:06.190 --> 00:57:08.550
Yeah, as always...

00:57:08.550 --> 00:57:15.200
Setting aside the shooting in Japan, the fact that Brian Woods has been killed means we're also still in danger!

00:57:15.200 --> 00:57:18.340
You always <i>did</i> worry too much...

00:57:18.340 --> 00:57:25.170
Even if I was just following your orders, I still regret what I did on the battlefield back then...

00:57:25.170 --> 00:57:28.450
What're you going on about now?!

00:57:28.840 --> 00:57:31.210
You lead a life of luxury <i>precisely</i> because you followed my orders, and took the Silver Star from Hunter! Don't forget it!

00:57:31.210 --> 00:57:35.260
You lead a life of luxury <i>precisely</i> because you followed my orders, and took the Silver Star from Hunter! Don't forget it!

00:57:35.260 --> 00:57:38.220
Y-Yes, sure. I-I'm sorry...

00:57:38.220 --> 00:57:44.730
Ah, forget it. Look. My family is going back to the US as soon as we get tickets.

00:57:45.220 --> 00:57:51.730
The Japanese police are useless. You'd better get out of here, too. Get on home, and quick.

00:57:51.730 --> 00:57:53.560
Yes, sir...

00:57:53.560 --> 00:57:55.950
I'll see you stateside.

00:58:00.140 --> 00:58:01.490
Mr Murphy?

00:58:02.610 --> 00:58:04.510
I'm at the front reception.

00:58:04.510 --> 00:58:06.540
We have a special delivery for you.

00:58:07.060 --> 00:58:09.790
Oh, right. Thank you.

00:58:10.510 --> 00:58:12.800
From Yokosuka Base?

00:58:12.800 --> 00:58:14.170
But who...?

00:58:14.170 --> 00:58:17.720
‘I know everything you did in the Middle East’?!

00:58:18.250 --> 00:58:19.430
What?!

00:58:19.430 --> 00:58:20.050
God…

00:58:21.010 --> 00:58:28.060
‘I don't want to cause a stir. But we need to look into Hunter's breach of Rule of Engagement’?!

00:58:28.060 --> 00:58:32.980
‘Your ticket is enclosed. Come to Tōkyō or face court-martial’?!

00:58:33.120 --> 00:58:37.670
‘Do not tell Waltz, and destroy this message immediately.’

00:58:37.670 --> 00:58:40.250
M-M-Mark Spencer?!

00:58:40.570 --> 00:58:45.330
‘Nikkō → Asakusa’

00:58:40.570 --> 00:58:43.100
Oh, Christ…

00:58:50.000 --> 00:58:55.910
It's really strange... It's the closest-range sniping yet, but they both missed once.

00:58:55.910 --> 00:58:56.510
Yeah...

00:58:56.510 --> 00:59:00.600
Maybe they were both nervous about facing another sniper.

00:59:01.020 --> 00:59:07.270
I'm concerned about all the snipings being near Asakusa too.

00:59:07.270 --> 00:59:08.060
Right...

00:59:08.060 --> 00:59:13.580
Maybe there's some other special meaning behind the dice, ranges and lines of fire...

00:59:13.580 --> 00:59:14.570
Oh!

00:59:17.240 --> 00:59:18.990
What is it, Jodie-<i>sensei</i>?

00:59:18.990 --> 00:59:23.120
We did that clinical autopsy of Hunter, like you suggested.

00:59:23.120 --> 00:59:28.850
There were a lot of painkillers in his stomach, really strong ones.

00:59:28.850 --> 00:59:30.620
Painkillers?

00:59:30.620 --> 00:59:34.800
And we found out why when we did an MRI of his skull.

00:59:34.800 --> 00:59:40.570
There was a bullet shard embedded near his brain stem. And it wasn't recent...

00:59:40.570 --> 00:59:43.180
The bullet he took in the war eight years ago, right?

00:59:43.180 --> 00:59:44.650
Yes.

00:59:44.650 --> 00:59:48.770
The removal was deemed a success,
 but a fragment must've been left behind.

00:59:48.770 --> 00:59:52.590
It would've put pressure on his
 nerves, especially his optic nerves.

00:59:52.590 --> 00:59:57.690
He would've suffered from frequent and intense migraines, and was probably nearly blind.

00:59:57.690 --> 01:00:02.700
Nearly blind? Must've been hard for him to snipe Woods in Seattle, then...

01:00:02.700 --> 01:00:06.290
What if the current sniper was behind that too?

01:00:07.280 --> 01:00:10.290
But then there's no reason for the showdown with Hunter...

01:00:10.290 --> 01:00:13.290
No. There's one possible reason.

01:00:15.340 --> 01:00:16.210
You can't mean...!

01:00:16.210 --> 01:00:17.390
Yeah.

01:00:17.390 --> 01:00:24.350
And if so, then there's another meaning behind the second Japanese sniping and the sniping of Hunter-<i>san</i>.

01:00:26.790 --> 01:00:28.180
Hi, this is Takagi.

01:00:28.180 --> 01:00:30.020
Oh! Conan-<i>kun</i>!

01:00:30.020 --> 01:00:37.140
You've got great timing. Could you tell Mouri-<i>san</i> that Lee-<i>san</i> actually happened to have an alibi, and also—

01:00:37.140 --> 01:00:39.530
Never mind him, what about Waltz-<i>san</i> and Murphy-<i>san</i>?

01:00:39.530 --> 01:00:42.570
Huh? Oh, Waltz-<i>san</i>'s still in Kyōto,

01:00:42.570 --> 01:00:46.530
but Murphy-<i>san</i> said he felt safe now, and left without a word to the local police guard

01:00:46.530 --> 01:00:50.730
boarding the Ōruri Express train leaving for Tōkyō at 9 AM.

01:00:50.730 --> 01:00:54.250
Apparently someone sent him a ticket, and he'd promised to see them.

01:00:54.250 --> 01:00:55.380
Sent him a ticket?!

01:00:55.380 --> 01:00:56.540
If he left at nine...!

01:00:56.540 --> 01:00:59.920
Apparently he's going to arrive at Asakusa Station at eleven.

01:00:59.920 --> 01:01:00.960
No!

01:01:00.960 --> 01:01:03.720
What if that was a trap set by the sniper?!

01:01:03.720 --> 01:01:06.720
He'd be watching the platform with the perfect sniping point!

01:01:06.720 --> 01:01:10.720
His target would even be sitting in the seat he picked!

01:01:10.720 --> 01:01:12.890
He's got to be near Asakusa Station!

01:01:13.380 --> 01:01:15.310
Anyway, we've got to hurry! There's only three minutes!

01:01:15.650 --> 01:01:16.810
This is bad! He's gonna go after Murphy!

01:01:16.810 --> 01:01:17.820
This is bad! He's gonna go after Murphy!

01:01:18.850 --> 01:01:21.320
Conan-<i>kun</i>?! What's going on, Conan-<i>kun</i>?!

01:01:27.430 --> 01:01:29.160
The express! It's already here?!

01:01:29.770 --> 01:01:31.790
That's right, it slows down for the bridge...

01:01:33.660 --> 01:01:36.420
What's that van stopped on that bridge...?

01:01:36.420 --> 01:01:38.290
Don't tell me...!

01:01:41.380 --> 01:01:42.340
A rifle!

01:01:44.840 --> 01:01:47.340
Don't tell me he's going to shoot from there?!

01:01:47.340 --> 01:01:49.430
There's no time to get back there!

01:01:57.150 --> 01:01:58.970
Conan-<i>kun</i>!

01:01:58.970 --> 01:02:03.070
Don't tell me he's going to shoot him while the train's in motion?!

01:02:11.410 --> 01:02:15.330
I've got to block the shot until the train passes!

01:02:21.180 --> 01:02:22.710
Please make it in time...

01:02:23.630 --> 01:02:25.970
Go!

01:02:49.890 --> 01:02:53.200
Hey! Over here, Murphy-<i>san</i>!

01:02:53.870 --> 01:02:55.700
{6\blur4.5}We will shortly be arriving at our destination, Asakusa Station...

01:02:55.700 --> 01:02:58.580
Come on, realise what's going on!

01:03:08.300 --> 01:03:09.340
Hey!

01:03:10.550 --> 01:03:11.930
No!

01:03:11.930 --> 01:03:15.430
Hey! Murphy-<i>san</i>!

01:03:18.980 --> 01:03:20.810
Conan-<i>kun</i>!

01:03:20.810 --> 01:03:22.310
Look out!

01:03:30.180 --> 01:03:31.740
Se... ra...

01:03:37.680 --> 01:03:38.330
Huh?

01:03:38.330 --> 01:03:39.590
What?

01:03:39.590 --> 01:03:40.960
What's that?

01:03:43.820 --> 01:03:45.710
Die!

01:04:02.020 --> 01:04:04.770
Sera! Hold on, Sera!

01:04:05.440 --> 01:04:07.190
How'd this end up happening...

01:04:07.890 --> 01:04:11.200
Damn! Damn! Damn!

01:04:13.740 --> 01:04:17.780
Goddamn!

01:04:27.450 --> 01:04:30.770
You're sure you're okay, you're not hurt?

01:04:31.130 --> 01:04:33.330
But there's blood on your clothes...

01:04:33.330 --> 01:04:34.950
It's not my blood...

01:04:34.950 --> 01:04:35.970
Conan-<i>kun</i>!

01:04:37.170 --> 01:04:38.270
Inspector Megure!

01:04:39.120 --> 01:04:40.640
Can we talk?

01:04:43.270 --> 01:04:47.450
{left channel only}#18, please head to counter five. #19… 

01:04:43.270 --> 01:04:45.660
I hate needles...

01:04:45.660 --> 01:04:47.450
Wanna go home?

01:04:47.450 --> 01:04:49.280
I wonder when Mum'll be back...

01:04:50.230 --> 01:04:56.040
So it wasn't a random murder — he was deliberately aiming for Murphy-<i>san</i>.

01:04:56.040 --> 01:04:57.040
Yeah.

01:04:57.040 --> 01:05:00.040
Thank you. We had to know for sure.

01:05:00.040 --> 01:05:04.040
So the sniper really <i>was</i> working with Hunter?

01:05:04.040 --> 01:05:06.100
Huh? What do you mean?

01:05:06.100 --> 01:05:11.420
Thanks to the FBI, some new facts have just come to light.

01:05:11.420 --> 01:05:13.680
New facts?

01:05:13.680 --> 01:05:22.560
We found the bullet that Hunter took to the head eight years ago left him in a state where he could no longer snipe anyone.

01:05:22.560 --> 01:05:29.070
Huh? But Hunter's diary suggested he was in a contest with the sniper...

01:05:29.070 --> 01:05:35.860
We believe that was all a lie,
 and he hired the sniper to shoot him.

01:05:35.860 --> 01:05:36.940
No way!

01:05:36.940 --> 01:05:38.070
But why...

01:05:38.070 --> 01:05:43.960
His death would throw the investigation into chaos, since he was the top suspect,

01:05:43.960 --> 01:05:48.630
and it would cause his next target, Murphy-<i>san</i>, 
to let his guard down so he could be sniped more easily.

01:05:48.630 --> 01:05:52.470
He probably planned everything out before he began.

01:05:52.470 --> 01:05:58.550
The reason he missed a shot when shooting Hunter, despite the short range of 150 metres,

01:05:58.550 --> 01:06:03.310
could have been from a moment
 of hesitation in killing his client.

01:06:03.770 --> 01:06:06.940
And we believe the sniper's use of smaller bullets from another gun,

01:06:07.650 --> 01:06:13.530
just for that sniping, was an expression of his desire to not hurt Hunter's corpse any more than necessary.

01:06:14.150 --> 01:06:15.740
I see...

01:06:15.740 --> 01:06:21.620
Then that means when Hunter fired back despite his bad eyes, it wasn't to try and shoot his sniper…

01:06:21.620 --> 01:06:25.420
It was a reply from Hunter, 
who'd sensed his sniper's hesitation...

01:06:25.420 --> 01:06:26.260
Yes.

01:06:26.260 --> 01:06:31.090
And that gives us an explanation for the mystery of why two skilled snipers

01:06:31.090 --> 01:06:37.050
each missed a shot despite facing one another at close range.

01:06:37.050 --> 01:06:42.810
But isn't it dangerous to decide all that just on circumstantial evidence?

01:06:42.810 --> 01:06:43.310
No...

01:06:45.170 --> 01:06:48.560
We have found evidence to back up these theories.

01:06:48.560 --> 01:06:49.540
Huh?!

01:06:49.540 --> 01:06:51.190
Evidence?

01:06:51.770 --> 01:06:59.700
When FBI HQ analysed the videos that Conan-<i>kun</i>'s friends took at the Bell Tree Tower, where the first sniping took place,

01:06:59.700 --> 01:07:05.830
we discovered they showed not just the culprit, but a suspected accomplice as well.

01:07:06.260 --> 01:07:07.640
It's true!

01:07:07.640 --> 01:07:09.400
There's two of them!

01:07:09.400 --> 01:07:15.790
Hunter probably accompanied the sniper, as a spotter for Fujinami-<i>san</i>'s sniping.  

01:07:13.530 --> 01:07:17.420
But the SEALs don't usually use spotters!

01:07:15.790 --> 01:07:23.310
{BG}I see. It wouldn't be a surprise if he had an accomplice to manage to carry out such a perfectly planned murder spree.  

01:07:17.420 --> 01:07:22.050
Was he nervous about it being his first sniping in Japan?

01:07:22.050 --> 01:07:23.310
Or perhaps...

01:07:23.820 --> 01:07:26.310
Suffering intense migraines and losing his sight...

01:07:26.310 --> 01:07:30.690
Hunter probably realised he'd never escape his pain as long as he lived,

01:07:30.690 --> 01:07:34.440
and hired the sniper to murder him and take revenge on his behalf.

01:07:34.440 --> 01:07:37.660
Hold on, there's still the riddle of the dice.

01:07:37.660 --> 01:07:38.750
Yes.

01:07:38.750 --> 01:07:44.790
We also found a shell and a die at the latest sniping position.

01:07:44.790 --> 01:07:46.620
How many dots on the die?

01:07:46.620 --> 01:07:51.370
Actually... It wasn't one, but five.

01:07:52.080 --> 01:07:52.880
What?!

01:07:53.530 --> 01:07:55.690
Wasn't it a countdown?

01:07:55.690 --> 01:08:00.300
Four, three, two, but then not one?!

01:08:00.300 --> 01:08:09.090
What's the meaning of this? We thought they were a message to Waltz-<i>san</i>, each dot vanishing representing a murder, but now?

01:08:09.090 --> 01:08:14.730
It seems we may have been too hasty in coming to our conclusions.

01:08:15.270 --> 01:08:22.260
There may be another reason he has to single out Waltz-<i>san</i>, instead of the men who made his family commit suicide.

01:08:22.260 --> 01:08:23.370
Anyway...

01:08:23.370 --> 01:08:25.700
Kevin Yoshino and Scott Green.

01:08:25.700 --> 01:08:28.540
Find out where they are immediately!

01:08:28.540 --> 01:08:33.040
They're sure to have some connection with this case! 

01:08:29.790 --> 01:08:31.060
No matter what happens...

01:08:31.060 --> 01:08:33.040
I won't let that sniper have his way!

01:08:33.040 --> 01:08:36.920
I'll stop the next sniping for sure!

01:08:33.580 --> 01:08:34.340
Got it?  

01:08:37.590 --> 01:08:44.180
Do you know anything about the Asakusa area or these dice?

01:08:44.180 --> 01:08:48.430
Like I told you, I don't care about Asakusa or dice or whatever!

01:08:48.430 --> 01:08:53.730
Just put out an arrest warrant for Scott Green! He's got to be the sniper!

01:08:53.730 --> 01:08:58.650
B-But at the moment, we don't have enough evidence...

01:08:58.650 --> 01:09:05.530
Honestly! Talking to you Japanese police is just a waste of time!

01:09:05.530 --> 01:09:06.410
Waltz-<i>san</i>.

01:09:07.730 --> 01:09:11.540
No matter what happens, promise me you won't go to Tōkyō.

01:09:11.540 --> 01:09:18.460
You just need to look at a map. The sniper will be already planning for his next murder in Asakusa.

01:09:18.980 --> 01:09:22.280
Who'd want to go somewhere as sinister as Tōkyō?!

01:09:22.280 --> 01:09:26.800
Just get me tickets to go back home from Kansai International Airport.

01:09:26.800 --> 01:09:32.640
Murphy told us the sniper's location at the cost of his own life.

01:09:32.640 --> 01:09:36.760
If I don't leave the country now,
 his death will have been for nothing!

01:09:36.760 --> 01:09:38.140
What a horrible man!

01:09:38.140 --> 01:09:40.780
His secretary's just been murdered!

01:09:44.000 --> 01:09:51.600
If someone's taken up Hunter's will, that means they must know about the crimes I committed eight years ago…

01:09:51.660 --> 01:09:54.830
Damn... I've got to do something!

01:09:56.000 --> 01:09:57.410
What the hell?

01:09:58.750 --> 01:10:00.430
Hello?

01:10:01.770 --> 01:10:04.760
Y-You!

01:10:08.430 --> 01:10:10.310
Conan-<i>kun</i>...

01:10:12.020 --> 01:10:14.430
We'll make sure to look after Sera-<i>san</i>.

01:10:14.430 --> 01:10:15.850
Right.

01:10:18.300 --> 01:10:23.650
Don't worry, she'll be fine. The doctor said her injuries aren't life-threatening.

01:10:23.650 --> 01:10:27.660
I'll let you know as soon as she wakes up, okay?

01:10:29.750 --> 01:10:31.030
Then see you tomorrow.

01:10:34.440 --> 01:10:37.540
Still, I'm glad nothing worse happened...

01:10:37.540 --> 01:10:41.660
If Sera-<i>san</i> hadn't been there for the brat, he'd have been in danger...

01:10:42.050 --> 01:10:45.670
She risked her life to protect Conan-<i>kun</i>...

01:10:46.770 --> 01:10:52.600
She really did put her life on the line. Remember what she said before?

01:10:52.720 --> 01:10:56.310
Don't worry! I'll make sure to protect Conan-<i>kun</i>.

01:10:56.900 --> 01:11:01.230
Not to mention, there's no bullet that can shoot through Conan-<i>kun</i>'s heart right now.

01:11:01.230 --> 01:11:04.320
Or your heart either, of course!

01:11:04.650 --> 01:11:09.820
That reminds me, she said there's no bullet that can shoot through your heart either, Ran...

01:11:09.820 --> 01:11:11.570
I can't forgive that sniper...

01:11:12.770 --> 01:11:17.870
For putting Conan-<i>kun</i> and Sera-<i>san</i> through all this...

01:11:17.870 --> 01:11:20.620
I'll never forgive him!

01:11:21.080 --> 01:11:22.440
Ran...

01:11:23.630 --> 01:11:29.350
Shū... ni... Shū-<i>nii</i>!{novel has first shortened and in katakana}

01:11:29.350 --> 01:11:31.010
‘Shū-nii’?

01:11:31.010 --> 01:11:36.280
Maybe she's calling for her late brother?
She mentioned she had a brother who'd died before...

01:11:36.280 --> 01:11:39.770
Huh? Was that bouquet there when we came in?

01:11:39.770 --> 01:11:40.940
Oh, you're right.

01:11:41.960 --> 01:11:44.240
Was someone else just here?

01:11:45.700 --> 01:11:47.260
Who's it from?

01:11:47.260 --> 01:11:48.470
I can't tell...

01:11:48.470 --> 01:11:51.800
But look, Sonoko, they're really beautiful!

01:11:51.800 --> 01:11:54.360
So they are! Let's put them on her windowsill.

01:11:54.360 --> 01:11:56.450
Yeah. I'll go and ask for a vase.

01:12:14.720 --> 01:12:16.130
What's wrong, Ran?

01:12:16.130 --> 01:12:19.060
Oh, it's nothing.

01:12:25.070 --> 01:12:27.690
Do we know where Green and Yoshino are?

01:12:27.690 --> 01:12:32.570
Apparently there's been reports of someone who looks like Green in the Kansai region,

01:12:33.280 --> 01:12:37.660
and a large-scale search has been started, centring on Ōsaka.

01:12:37.660 --> 01:12:41.210
Maybe he intends to target Waltz-<i>san</i> on the way to Kansai International Airport after all...

01:12:41.210 --> 01:12:42.560
This isn't good.

01:12:42.960 --> 01:12:51.200
The timing's too perfect. What if he's a decoy to draw attention away from Yoshino?

01:12:53.110 --> 01:12:54.220
It's Inspector Megure.

01:12:55.550 --> 01:12:56.410
Yes?

01:12:56.410 --> 01:12:58.720
James-<i>san</i>, I have some news for you.

01:12:58.720 --> 01:13:02.990
What is it? If you mean the reports about Green, I've already heard about those from Camel.

01:13:02.990 --> 01:13:09.160
No, something even worse. Waltz-<i>san</i> vanished.

01:13:09.160 --> 01:13:11.280
W-What?!

01:13:11.280 --> 01:13:14.240
We were just as surprised...

01:13:14.240 --> 01:13:17.240
According to the Kyōto Police, after they questioned him,

01:13:17.240 --> 01:13:22.960
he told his wife he'd be back tomorrow, and left his hotel through a back door...

01:13:22.960 --> 01:13:25.380
But why?! What possible reason could he have?!

01:13:25.380 --> 01:13:27.660
Looks like something's happened.

01:13:26.170 --> 01:13:30.880
Yes, right. I'll be in touch the moment we discover anything new.  

01:13:27.660 --> 01:13:28.950
Yeah.

01:13:36.040 --> 01:13:43.390
What is it, Jodie-<i>sensei</i>? Yeah, I already had Detective Takagi tell me about the reports of Green being spotted.

01:13:43.390 --> 01:13:45.890
Yeah, and then?

01:13:46.090 --> 01:13:48.150
What?! Waltz-<i>san</i>?!

01:13:48.590 --> 01:13:50.940
I wonder what he could be thinking...

01:13:50.940 --> 01:13:58.210
If we figure out the riddle of the dice the sniper left behind, we should be able to tell where Waltz-<i>san</i> is headed...

01:13:58.210 --> 01:14:01.950
You mean he's going to the site of the next sniping?

01:14:02.080 --> 01:14:03.690
I don't know...

01:14:03.690 --> 01:14:12.800
But there might be a special connection between the sniper and Waltz-<i>san</i> — something that we don't know yet.

01:14:12.800 --> 01:14:17.800
Right. I'll check through the connections between the victims and the suspects again.

01:14:17.800 --> 01:14:20.400
Okay, I'll call you again later.

01:14:21.800 --> 01:14:24.540
Sorry for the wait, Camel! Let's go.

01:14:24.540 --> 01:14:25.750
Right.

01:14:25.750 --> 01:14:28.770
We'll meet up with Investigation Division One, and go over everything once again.

01:14:28.770 --> 01:14:30.860
Right. I'm counting on you.

01:14:38.030 --> 01:14:42.790
Waltz-<i>san</i> told his wife that he'd be back tomorrow.

01:14:42.790 --> 01:14:51.810
That means there's going to be another sniping in the next 24 hours!

01:15:17.950 --> 01:15:23.200
I got everything you wanted. All untraceable.

01:15:23.200 --> 01:15:25.020
And the scopes?

01:15:25.020 --> 01:15:27.080
All adjusted.

01:15:27.080 --> 01:15:30.120
Hah, I expected nothing less from you, Carlos.

01:15:30.120 --> 01:15:32.590
You are the best, after all...

01:15:32.590 --> 01:15:34.250
You and Hunter, that is.

01:15:34.250 --> 01:15:38.600
How 'bout I let you take out the shooter this time?

01:15:38.600 --> 01:15:41.470
Then you'll truly be number one.

01:15:41.470 --> 01:15:46.230
Weren't you one kill behind Hunter's record in the war?

01:15:46.470 --> 01:15:51.020
Rear Admiral Spencer's orders were just to procure the weapon.

01:15:51.650 --> 01:15:53.030
Never mind.

01:15:53.030 --> 01:15:56.630
If I know the target, I don't need your help anyway.

01:15:56.630 --> 01:15:58.790
Thanks for the gun.

01:15:58.790 --> 01:16:01.700
I have a message from Admiral Spencer.

01:16:02.140 --> 01:16:06.960
He says there will be no inquiry into the origin of the shooting spree.

01:16:07.500 --> 01:16:10.050
Just eliminate the sniper at all costs.

01:16:10.050 --> 01:16:12.710
Preserve the credibility of the US Military!

01:16:13.170 --> 01:16:15.340
The origin of the shooting spree?

01:16:15.340 --> 01:16:17.210
How much does the admiral know?

01:16:17.210 --> 01:16:19.590
Probably... everything.

01:16:19.590 --> 01:16:22.050
What?! But how?!

01:16:22.050 --> 01:16:27.520
Only one person alive knows about
 that operation, and that's me!

01:16:27.520 --> 01:16:32.060
The sniper used the admiral's name to threaten Bill Murphy.

01:16:32.060 --> 01:16:34.060
Murphy was scared.

01:16:34.060 --> 01:16:39.790
The day before he was killed,
 he asked for a reduction of charges.

01:16:39.790 --> 01:16:48.040
He e-mailed the admiral, confessed — the plan to steal Hunter's Silver Star, your orders afterward, everything!

01:16:48.640 --> 01:16:49.830
What?!

01:16:49.830 --> 01:16:54.620
Your crimes from eight years ago... They're unforgivable.

01:16:54.620 --> 01:16:55.710
But...

01:16:55.710 --> 01:17:03.090
We have to stop a former American soldier from committing any more murders on foreign soil.

01:17:04.680 --> 01:17:07.740
Well, if he knows everything anyway...

01:17:07.740 --> 01:17:14.630
Please tell the admiral... After this case is settled, I'd like a meeting.

01:17:14.630 --> 01:17:16.150
There's one more thing.

01:17:16.150 --> 01:17:16.860
What?

01:17:16.860 --> 01:17:19.570
Did you figure out the meaning behind the dice?

01:17:20.780 --> 01:17:24.570
Why bother? They're irrelevant now we know the shooter.

01:17:27.580 --> 01:17:30.750
And now for some breaking news.

01:17:30.750 --> 01:17:37.880
Bill Murphy-<i>san</i>, who was sniped to death aboard the Tohto Railways Ōruri Express at 11 AM yesterday,

01:17:37.880 --> 01:17:42.880
has been linked to the previously murdered Timothy Hunter-<i>san</i>.

01:17:43.720 --> 01:17:50.770
Also, the girl who was injured in the sniping is also expected to make a full recovery. And that's the end of the breaking news.

01:17:50.770 --> 01:17:54.560
<i>The sniping spree is set to continue?!
</i>

01:17:50.770 --> 01:17:54.560
Huh? So it wasn't a completely random killing spree then!

01:17:54.560 --> 01:18:01.800
I did warn you! Your careless remark had the whole of Tōkyō panicking for the last two days!

01:18:01.800 --> 01:18:05.450
Oh, really? Well, sorry about that...

01:18:05.450 --> 01:18:09.460
Geez... What a troublemaker.

01:18:09.460 --> 01:18:10.620
Uncle!

01:18:10.620 --> 01:18:13.410
Apparently Sera-<i>neechan</i> woke up.

01:18:13.410 --> 01:18:16.580
We're all going to visit her...

01:18:16.580 --> 01:18:22.300
Sorry, but you'll have to go without me.
 I've still got some thinking to do about this...

01:18:22.300 --> 01:18:25.900
Old man, you've been up all night thinking about the case?

01:18:22.780 --> 01:18:27.850
And if my theory about the last die is right, I've solved the riddle of the dice!

01:18:27.850 --> 01:18:28.970
What?! Really?!

01:18:28.970 --> 01:18:34.770
Huh? Yeah! One night's more than enough for a Great Detective like me to solve this!

01:18:34.770 --> 01:18:37.440
So what do they mean?

01:18:37.440 --> 01:18:40.190
They're... a countdown!

01:18:40.190 --> 01:18:40.690
...Huh?

01:18:40.690 --> 01:18:48.200
The bridge must've shook. And so the last die changed from a one to a five!

01:18:48.200 --> 01:18:51.780
See? Once you realise that, everything fits—

01:18:51.780 --> 01:18:55.200
Huh?! Where'd that brat go?!

01:18:55.200 --> 01:18:59.930
That's not a countdown. There's another meaning to it.

01:19:00.460 --> 01:19:04.880
I should get there quickly and go over what happened yesterday with Sera.

01:19:10.890 --> 01:19:14.140
Here! A clear line of fire...

01:19:14.140 --> 01:19:16.890
Yes, I've found it!

01:19:16.890 --> 01:19:21.390
The perfect position to target Chigusa...

01:19:22.330 --> 01:19:25.420
Hah! The game is mine!

01:19:28.160 --> 01:19:30.540
Y-You!

01:19:30.540 --> 01:19:34.290
I've taken care of Murphy. Now it is your turn.

01:19:34.290 --> 01:19:37.290
W-Why? Why you?!

01:19:37.290 --> 01:19:39.210
Is it the money?

01:19:39.210 --> 01:19:41.930
How much did he pay? I'll double it!

01:19:41.930 --> 01:19:44.080
You never change, Waltz.

01:19:44.080 --> 01:19:44.880
I... uhh...

01:19:45.550 --> 01:19:52.870
Look, let's make a deal. You, here in a foreign country… You could use some cash, right?

01:19:52.870 --> 01:19:59.150
Tomorrow night, come to Chigusa in Asakusa at 8 PM sharp. We'll discuss it then.

01:19:59.150 --> 01:20:04.010
Uh, yeah, okay. Chigusa in Asakusa...

01:20:04.010 --> 01:20:09.700
If you confess everything... Admit your guilt... I'll let you live.

01:20:09.700 --> 01:20:16.490
However, if you're even late, say goodbye to your family!{XTL from JP: But, if you don't come, or if you even happen to be late... know that your family will die. Got it?!}

01:20:16.490 --> 01:20:18.040
Understood?{XTL from JP: But, if you don't come, or if you even happen to be late... know that your family will die. Got it?!}

01:20:18.040 --> 01:20:21.330
Hello? Hello? Hey, I...

01:20:21.330 --> 01:20:23.040
Argh, damn it!

01:20:24.860 --> 01:20:27.760
Helen... Sarah...

01:20:27.760 --> 01:20:28.510
Waltz-<i>san</i>!

01:20:28.510 --> 01:20:29.880
We've got a problem!

01:20:29.880 --> 01:20:33.760
Scott Green's been spotted by
 the cameras at Shin-Ōsaka Station!

01:20:33.760 --> 01:20:36.510
It's too dangerous to go to Kansai International Airport at the moment!

01:20:36.510 --> 01:20:39.520
I'm sorry, but you'll have to abandon your plans to leave Japan tomorrow.

01:20:40.790 --> 01:20:45.150
Damn! Then it's kill or be killed.

01:20:47.730 --> 01:20:51.240
Here, the perfect position to target Chigusa.

01:20:51.240 --> 01:20:53.950
He'll pick this spot — it's textbook!

01:20:53.950 --> 01:20:55.240
Any sniper's dream!

01:20:55.240 --> 01:21:00.500
But tonight it's not <i>me</i> that's going to be the target — it's <i>him</i>!{novel has all of this as one thought, movie starts it as spoken but switches to thought, but I can't tell when}

01:21:00.950 --> 01:21:04.670
Takes a sniper to beat a sniper...

01:21:07.390 --> 01:21:10.210
It all comes down to second-guessing...

01:21:10.210 --> 01:21:15.010
Anticipating your opponent's moves, gaining tactical advantage...

01:21:15.010 --> 01:21:19.430
Most of all, superior position guarantees victory.

01:21:19.430 --> 01:21:22.770
The fact that I have found this position means...

01:21:22.770 --> 01:21:25.770
Victory is mine!

01:21:25.770 --> 01:21:28.820
You challenge me, you lose!

01:21:28.820 --> 01:21:32.040
Say ‘hi’ to Hunter in Hell!

01:21:34.160 --> 01:21:37.290
Huh? Conan-<i>kun</i>, you're here all by yourself?

01:21:37.290 --> 01:21:39.910
Yeah, everyone else is coming by car.

01:21:39.910 --> 01:21:41.290
Ah.

01:21:41.290 --> 01:21:45.220
I was just about to go to the shop downstairs, want to come with me?

01:21:45.220 --> 01:21:46.920
Nah, I'll wait here.

01:21:48.080 --> 01:21:49.470
Okay, let's go, Sonoko!

01:21:49.470 --> 01:21:52.490
Right! Sera-<i>san</i>, we're heading out for a bit.

01:21:52.490 --> 01:21:55.000
Okay, thank you.

01:21:52.920 --> 01:21:55.000
We'll be back before long.

01:21:55.000 --> 01:21:56.680
Let us know if something happens.

01:21:56.680 --> 01:21:58.680
Sure!

01:21:59.140 --> 01:22:00.730
Hi, Conan-<i>kun</i>.

01:22:00.730 --> 01:22:04.530
Looks like the bullet really didn't hit you.

01:22:07.000 --> 01:22:09.570
I never got a chance to thank you for saving me...

01:22:09.570 --> 01:22:13.990
Don't worry, I was just keeping my promise with Ran-<i>kun</i>.

01:22:13.990 --> 01:22:15.570
But what about the sniper...?

01:22:15.570 --> 01:22:19.560
Both of the suspects are still in hiding...

01:22:19.560 --> 01:22:20.240
Is that so?

01:22:21.110 --> 01:22:24.830
Yesterday, I noticed something when I was shot...

01:22:25.690 --> 01:22:29.340
The sniper was using a laser sight at the time.

01:22:29.340 --> 01:22:31.710
Isn't that strange?

01:22:31.710 --> 01:22:37.840
Snipers don't usually use them — their targets would realise they're being targeted, and they can even give away their location.

01:22:38.280 --> 01:22:43.240
I get it. That's why Hunter faked that shootout instead of committing suicide...

01:22:43.240 --> 01:22:45.020
Huh? What do you mean?

01:22:45.020 --> 01:22:48.310
If he'd committed suicide, the investigation would've been completely called off,

01:22:48.310 --> 01:22:50.940
and Murphy-<i>san</i> and Waltz-<i>san</i>

01:22:52.050 --> 01:22:53.900
But he didn't.

01:22:53.900 --> 01:23:02.800
I get it. That was a final test for the killer, he was making him into a true cold-blooded sniper!

01:23:02.940 --> 01:23:04.280
Yeah.

01:23:04.620 --> 01:23:08.820
The first sniping was the maximum range for an MK11.

01:23:08.820 --> 01:23:11.780
The second sniping was a moving target at night.

01:23:11.780 --> 01:23:16.470
And the third sniping was to check that no emotions could ever change his mind.

01:23:17.100 --> 01:23:22.420
Hunter was making his killer into the ultimate sniper, right up until his death!

01:23:22.420 --> 01:23:23.390
Then that means the sniper is—

01:23:24.390 --> 01:23:25.930
Are you okay?

01:23:25.930 --> 01:23:28.220
Yeah, I'll be fine...

01:23:28.360 --> 01:23:30.810
Hey! We've come over for a visit!

01:23:30.810 --> 01:23:33.500
Hey, Genta-<i>kun</i>, you're being too loud...

01:23:33.500 --> 01:23:34.570
Oh, sorry...

01:23:34.570 --> 01:23:35.820
Oh, Conan-<i>kun</i>!

01:23:35.820 --> 01:23:38.120
What's all that stuff you guys brought?

01:23:38.120 --> 01:23:40.180
Something really amazing!

01:23:40.180 --> 01:23:40.610
Right!

01:23:40.610 --> 01:23:43.530
We thought it might help cheer her up. Right?

01:23:44.360 --> 01:23:45.340
Right!

01:23:45.340 --> 01:23:46.040
Huh?

01:23:46.620 --> 01:23:49.040
Wow, that's great!

01:23:49.040 --> 01:23:51.580
You made that all by yourselves?

01:23:51.580 --> 01:23:52.820
Yeah!

01:23:52.820 --> 01:23:55.080
It's for our summer homework project!

01:23:55.080 --> 01:23:57.480
It's not exactly finished yet...

01:23:57.480 --> 01:23:59.090
...but we wanted to show it to you!

01:23:59.090 --> 01:24:00.660
Thanks!

01:24:00.660 --> 01:24:02.290
It really is great!

01:24:02.290 --> 01:24:03.850
Yeah, it's very well-made.

01:24:03.850 --> 01:24:08.890
They may not be the same shapes as the real buildings, but they're the same sizes and in the right places!

01:24:08.890 --> 01:24:11.310
Ai-<i>chan</i> checked all of them!

01:24:11.310 --> 01:24:13.340
Okay, that's the last one!  

01:24:12.010 --> 01:24:16.570
Though <i>one of us</i> hasn't bothered to help with anything at all.

01:24:13.340 --> 01:24:14.930
Yay, it's all done!  

01:24:14.930 --> 01:24:16.570
It's not finished, but it is complete!  

01:24:16.570 --> 01:24:19.180
You've done all that, but it's not finished?

01:24:19.180 --> 01:24:21.370
It looks good just like that.

01:24:21.370 --> 01:24:22.490
What's left to do?

01:24:22.490 --> 01:24:25.160
We gotta paint 'em...

01:24:25.160 --> 01:24:30.210
But we only had a chance to take photos of the west side when we were at the Bell Tree,

01:24:30.210 --> 01:24:32.500
so we don't know what colours the rest should be.

01:24:32.500 --> 01:24:36.190
We would've liked to go up one more time before we start painting it, but well...

01:24:36.190 --> 01:24:37.880
Then why don't we take another look?

01:24:37.880 --> 01:24:42.490
It hasn't reopened yet, but the repairs are all done, so you could have the whole tower to yourselves!

01:24:42.490 --> 01:24:43.740
Really?!

01:24:43.740 --> 01:24:44.760
You mean it?!

01:24:44.760 --> 01:24:46.410
Yay!

01:24:45.850 --> 01:24:49.020
{left speaker only}But Sonoko, they haven't caught the sniper yet, have they?

01:24:47.070 --> 01:24:49.020
What is it?

01:24:49.020 --> 01:24:53.270
That'll make our summer homework project perfect!

01:24:49.870 --> 01:24:53.270
{left speaker only}It's fine! Do you really think he'd
 turn up at the same place twice?

01:24:53.270 --> 01:24:57.740
{main}Haibara... That model's got the right scale, right?

01:24:54.890 --> 01:24:59.030
{left speaker only}And even the TV said that it's not actually a random killing spree after all!

01:24:57.740 --> 01:24:59.030
{main}Yes.

01:24:59.030 --> 01:25:02.780
Okay! Then let's hurry back and get our cameras!

01:25:02.780 --> 01:25:03.670
Yeah!

01:25:03.670 --> 01:25:05.940
Huh? What is it, Conan-<i>kun</i>?

01:25:05.940 --> 01:25:06.280
Huh?

01:25:06.280 --> 01:25:08.240
What's this feeling?

01:25:08.240 --> 01:25:11.290
I feel like I just spotted something
 I couldn't see before on a map...

01:25:11.290 --> 01:25:14.710
Hey, make sure you help us paint it, you hear?

01:25:14.710 --> 01:25:16.960
What is it, Conan-<i>kun</i>?

01:25:16.960 --> 01:25:18.460
What is it?

01:25:18.460 --> 01:25:20.460
Did you spot something, Conan?

01:25:23.500 --> 01:25:24.920
Wow, that's interesting!

01:25:24.920 --> 01:25:26.510
Huh? What is?

01:25:26.510 --> 01:25:32.940
If you look at it from down here, it looks like some of the buildings we made are the same height!

01:25:34.090 --> 01:25:35.530
Conan-<i>kun</i>!

01:25:35.530 --> 01:25:37.720
Genta... Sorry, but can you show me?

01:25:37.720 --> 01:25:39.020
Huh? Take a look.

01:25:39.020 --> 01:25:40.500
Wow, you're right!

01:25:40.500 --> 01:25:41.940
That is interesting!

01:25:41.940 --> 01:25:46.950
{BG}That's because things close to you look bigger than things in the distance.  

01:25:42.400 --> 01:25:46.950
I get it! That message wasn't supposed to be seen in two dimensions...

01:25:47.610 --> 01:25:50.950
...but something you have to see in 3D!

01:25:51.470 --> 01:25:52.800
Here!

01:25:52.800 --> 01:25:56.960
If you look from here, the height of the first and second sniping positions match!

01:25:57.580 --> 01:25:59.750
What about the others?!

01:26:00.210 --> 01:26:04.470
The third was a floating platform, and the fourth was Komagata Bridge...

01:26:04.470 --> 01:26:08.110
If I add those and look at all of them from the same place...

01:26:08.110 --> 01:26:09.260
It's an isosceles trapezium!

01:26:09.690 --> 01:26:14.270
Hold on... If I add the observation deck of the Bell Tree Tower, right in the middle...

01:26:16.710 --> 01:26:18.770
It's a pentagon!

01:26:19.460 --> 01:26:25.990
This shape wouldn't just appear by chance! It had to have been planned intentionally!

01:26:26.970 --> 01:26:30.100
Ran-<i>neechan</i>! I've got to go, I forgot something!

01:26:30.100 --> 01:26:34.390
H-Hey! Conan-<i>kun</i>! Don't you want to go to the Bell Tree?!

01:26:33.330 --> 01:26:36.290
What, you're running off on us again?! 

01:26:34.390 --> 01:26:36.290
Be careful, Conan-<i>kun</i>...

01:26:36.290 --> 01:26:38.900
No, I'll pass for today!

01:27:04.410 --> 01:27:07.940
When he vanished, Waltz-<i>san</i> said he'd be back in Kyōto today.

01:27:07.940 --> 01:27:12.870
That means he'll have to finish up here by around 8 PM so he can get on the bullet train{shinkansen}.

01:27:12.870 --> 01:27:15.570
Damn, I gotta hurry!

01:27:16.370 --> 01:27:19.120
Hi, Cool Kid. I've got new info.

01:27:19.670 --> 01:27:22.500
The Ōsaka Police have arrested Scott Green.

01:27:23.440 --> 01:27:30.390
Apparently Hunter asked him to sneak into Ōsaka and avoid being caught until just now.

01:27:30.390 --> 01:27:30.890
Then like I thought...

01:27:31.380 --> 01:27:36.810
Yes. Apparently he did have some notion that Hunter was in Japan to enact his revenge,

01:27:36.980 --> 01:27:38.640
but when he actually saw him and the determination on his face,

01:27:39.310 --> 01:27:42.980
he decided to help him achieve the closure on his life that he desired so much.

01:27:43.070 --> 01:27:45.810
If he was a decoy, then the sniper must be...

01:27:45.810 --> 01:27:46.480
Yeah!

01:27:46.480 --> 01:27:50.110
Oh, and I've got some new intel from FBI HQ as well.

01:27:50.110 --> 01:27:56.890
Apparently there were reports of Hunter living with an Asian man after he lost his family!

01:27:56.890 --> 01:28:00.290
And if that man was Kevin Yoshino...

01:28:00.290 --> 01:28:02.800
Then he could be behind it all!

01:28:02.800 --> 01:28:05.250
Yeah. Thanks, Jodie-<i>sensei</i>.

01:28:05.250 --> 01:28:07.460
By the way, where are you now, Conan-<i>kun</i>?

01:28:07.460 --> 01:28:10.460
I'm heading to what I think is the next sniping position.

01:28:10.460 --> 01:28:12.940
What?! You solved the riddle of the dice?!

01:28:12.940 --> 01:28:17.140
No, I can't be sure yet, so I'm headed to check, but there's no time...

01:28:17.140 --> 01:28:19.500
Is there any way I can help?

01:28:19.500 --> 01:28:24.440
If my deduction is right, the observation deck of the Bell Tree Tower will be involved again.

01:28:24.440 --> 01:28:25.400
The Bell Tree...

01:28:25.930 --> 01:28:28.500
Okay! We'll head there now!

01:28:28.500 --> 01:28:28.900
Right.

01:28:28.900 --> 01:28:31.220
Just make sure to be careful!

01:28:31.490 --> 01:28:32.550
Let's go.

01:28:32.550 --> 01:28:33.820
Right!

01:28:41.710 --> 01:28:44.790
From the model, it should be somewhere around here...

01:28:46.250 --> 01:28:48.050
From the top of that building...

01:28:48.500 --> 01:28:50.260
You might be able to see it!

01:29:03.600 --> 01:29:05.360
Where's the Bell Tree?!

01:29:13.230 --> 01:29:17.790
The building where he shot Fujinami-<i>san</i>
 and the building where he shot Yasuhara-<i>san</i>...

01:29:18.820 --> 01:29:22.410
It's just like I thought with the
 model — they make a horizontal line!

01:29:22.410 --> 01:29:24.670
And that means...

01:29:25.040 --> 01:29:30.190
If I connect up the positions for the third and fourth snipings, it's an isosceles trapezium...

01:29:30.190 --> 01:29:33.430
And if I add the first observation deck of the Bell Tree Tower...

01:29:33.430 --> 01:29:36.850
That's definitely a pentagon!

01:29:37.470 --> 01:29:44.080
If I consider the dice left at each sniping position too, and put the remaining faces at the Bell Tree Tower...

01:29:45.950 --> 01:29:49.340
I get it, so that's what it means!

01:29:49.950 --> 01:29:54.300
What the sniper wanted to show Waltz-<i>san</i>, his last target...

01:29:54.300 --> 01:29:55.200
Was a star!

01:29:55.810 --> 01:30:00.270
A star that represents that Silver Star stolen from Hunter!

01:30:00.270 --> 01:30:06.130
Hunter and the sniper intended for Waltz-<i>san</i> to see this star, the Silver Star, from the very beginning!

01:30:06.830 --> 01:30:07.840
{***this section is all thought in novel, but first bit is spoken in movie}And that means...

01:30:07.840 --> 01:30:13.420
There's been a ‘one’ die at the first observation deck of the Bell Tree Tower all along,

01:30:13.420 --> 01:30:17.430
and the sniping position for the sniper's next murder is the first observation deck too!

01:30:17.430 --> 01:30:18.430
There!

01:30:18.430 --> 01:30:20.720
So the sniper really was...

01:30:21.480 --> 01:30:23.430
Kevin Yoshino!

01:30:23.430 --> 01:30:26.270
Damn! Where's he aiming at?!

01:30:27.120 --> 01:30:32.680
A slightly taller building would be able to see the star better...

01:30:32.680 --> 01:30:34.650
That must be where Waltz-<i>san</i> is going...

01:30:34.650 --> 01:30:35.860
There?!

01:30:40.200 --> 01:30:43.590
Say ‘hi’ to Hunter in Hell!

01:30:44.120 --> 01:30:46.040
Come on, Waltz.

01:30:46.040 --> 01:30:47.620
Come to the window...

01:30:47.620 --> 01:30:51.880
The mo{r}ment you decipher our message will be your last!

01:30:54.510 --> 01:30:57.010
This time I'm going to stop you for sure!

01:30:58.090 --> 01:31:00.640
Today I'll finally be rid of Hunter's ghost...

01:31:00.640 --> 01:31:02.930
Settle the score, once and for all!

01:31:03.470 --> 01:31:05.370
W-W-What the...?!

01:31:05.800 --> 01:31:08.710
T-That wasn't here before...

01:31:09.680 --> 01:31:12.980
Did they leave this for me to see?!

01:31:14.270 --> 01:31:17.470
Go!

01:31:20.210 --> 01:31:21.070
Die!

01:31:35.800 --> 01:31:36.970
What?!

01:31:36.970 --> 01:31:38.840
That flash…

01:31:39.560 --> 01:31:42.800
It came from that building...

01:31:45.680 --> 01:31:48.100
That kid, interfering again?!

01:31:49.770 --> 01:31:51.270
Crap!

01:31:52.220 --> 01:31:52.940
You…

01:31:53.470 --> 01:31:55.720
You'll pay for that!

01:31:55.720 --> 01:31:56.610
You brat!

01:31:59.030 --> 01:32:01.320
Damn, there's nowhere to hide on this roof!

01:32:12.250 --> 01:32:14.200
M-My leg...!

01:32:19.950 --> 01:32:21.260
Oh, crap…

01:32:21.260 --> 01:32:22.890
You twerp!

01:32:22.890 --> 01:32:25.980
You ruined everything! Everything!

01:32:41.700 --> 01:32:43.700
No way! He was sniped?!

01:32:43.700 --> 01:32:47.580
But where could someone even target somewhere that high?!

01:32:47.580 --> 01:32:49.080
From there?!

01:32:54.510 --> 01:32:57.180
Another sniper?!

01:32:58.340 --> 01:33:00.300
But how?!

01:33:00.300 --> 01:33:05.850
The only place with a shot is Asakusa Sky Court...

01:33:05.850 --> 01:33:08.180
But that building is...{too far}

01:33:08.560 --> 01:33:11.780
Finally, if you shoot from the Bell Tree here, you'll be safe.

01:33:11.780 --> 01:33:17.020
But what if Waltz figures out the Silver Star message and targets me from the Asakusa Sky Court...?

01:33:17.020 --> 01:33:18.730
Relax...

01:33:18.730 --> 01:33:23.990
The one sniper who could make such an distant, upward shot is gone.

01:33:24.820 --> 01:33:28.090
O-Oh, right. Your eyes, Tim...

01:33:28.090 --> 01:33:32.160
No. I'd never have been able to pull off a shot with this long a range.

01:33:33.000 --> 01:33:35.140
Are you saying there was a better sniper than you, Tim?

01:33:35.140 --> 01:33:37.170
Yeah, in the FBI.

01:33:37.170 --> 01:33:40.710
They had a sniper with amazing skills, dubbed the ‘Silver Bullet’.

01:33:40.710 --> 01:33:46.930
But you've got nothing to worry about. 
He's missing, presumed dead.

01:33:47.980 --> 01:33:50.680
I-Impossible... It was him?! {and suddenly the movie gives up on english}

01:33:51.420 --> 01:33:54.690
The Silver Bullet actually appeared?!

01:33:56.270 --> 01:33:57.690
Subaru-<i>san</i>?!

01:33:58.400 --> 01:33:59.940
Why is he there?!

01:34:01.120 --> 01:34:06.180
I see. Subaru-<i>san</i> figured out the riddle of the dice too!

01:34:06.700 --> 01:34:11.450
Conan-<i>kun</i>! We're at the Bell Tree. We're asking to be let up there now.

01:34:11.450 --> 01:34:16.460
Great. Head straight to the roof of the observation deck! Yoshino's there!

01:34:16.460 --> 01:34:18.630
Then he really was the sniper.

01:34:18.630 --> 01:34:20.840
Yeah. So how about it, can you get up there?

01:34:22.080 --> 01:34:25.340
No luck! Apparently the owners have it reserved for today, they won't let us in!

01:34:25.340 --> 01:34:27.130
No luck! Apparently the owners have it reserved for today, they won't let us in!

01:34:27.130 --> 01:34:28.350
That's right...!

01:34:28.350 --> 01:34:31.350
Jodie-<i>sensei</i>! It's Ran and my friends up there!

01:34:31.920 --> 01:34:35.600
Explain what's going on, come up to the observation deck and arrest Yoshino!

01:34:35.600 --> 01:34:39.730
Got it! I'll get Inspector Megure to make them let us in!

01:34:40.530 --> 01:34:42.950
Wow, it's really beautiful!

01:34:42.950 --> 01:34:46.360
Isn't it? The Bell Tree has the best views at night too!

01:34:46.360 --> 01:34:47.700
It's so cool!

01:34:47.700 --> 01:34:49.560
It's even prettier at night!

01:34:49.560 --> 01:34:51.370
That's right!

01:34:51.370 --> 01:34:54.490
Now, let's go to the other side we haven't photographed yet!

01:34:54.490 --> 01:34:55.220
Yeah!

01:34:55.220 --> 01:34:56.120
Let's go!

01:34:59.490 --> 01:35:01.380
S-Shin'ichi?

01:35:03.630 --> 01:35:06.130
So that shot didn't completely neutralise him?

01:35:10.480 --> 01:35:13.220
I've come so far, I can't give up now!

01:35:13.220 --> 01:35:16.260
I promised Hunter-<i>san</i>...

01:35:18.210 --> 01:35:20.140
Good. You've improved.

01:35:20.140 --> 01:35:22.770
Now all you need is actual experience.

01:35:22.770 --> 01:35:27.890
Right! I'll start with Brian Woods. And I'll make Waltz pay...!

01:35:27.890 --> 01:35:29.410
Are you really sure about this?

01:35:29.410 --> 01:35:29.910
Huh?

01:35:29.910 --> 01:35:34.540
It's a bit late to worry about it now, but I regret getting you involved...

01:35:34.540 --> 01:35:36.330
What's got into you, Tim?

01:35:36.330 --> 01:35:40.210
You saved my life so many times out there on the front line.

01:35:40.210 --> 01:35:43.530
And now, I finally have a chance to repay you!

01:35:43.530 --> 01:35:44.710
Still...

01:35:44.710 --> 01:35:48.630
And I can never forgive Waltz and Murphy.

01:35:48.630 --> 01:35:56.160
He falsely accused you and took away your Silver Star just because your deeds were overshadowing his!

01:35:56.160 --> 01:36:02.730
And then just when we asked for the case to be re-opened, he ordered Murphy to kill you!

01:36:11.550 --> 01:36:13.620
Yeah, that's right...

01:36:13.620 --> 01:36:20.010
If you hadn't had your suspicions and compared the surgically removed bullet with Murphy's gun,

01:36:20.010 --> 01:36:22.130
the truth would've stayed forever in the dark.

01:36:22.130 --> 01:36:26.710
But then they even stole the proof out from under us, and we couldn't do a thing!

01:36:26.710 --> 01:36:29.170
Kevin, I'll say this one last time.

01:36:29.170 --> 01:36:35.640
Avenge my wife and sister, and send Waltz and everyone who destroyed my life straight to Hell!

01:36:35.640 --> 01:36:37.640
Sure! I promise!

01:36:37.640 --> 01:36:39.350
I'll do it!

01:36:39.350 --> 01:36:42.560
I'll make sure to send them all to Hell!

01:36:43.270 --> 01:36:44.480
I'm counting on you!

01:36:44.730 --> 01:36:48.380
That's right. I can't give up now!

01:36:48.380 --> 01:36:51.490
I can still get away if I use my escape plan...!

01:36:51.490 --> 01:36:54.490
And Waltz has to pay!

01:36:54.490 --> 01:36:57.490
Right! So you have to get everyone out of there right now!

01:36:58.330 --> 01:36:59.470
But what about the sniper?

01:36:59.470 --> 01:37:02.420
Don't worry! The FBI are coming up to deal with him!

01:37:02.420 --> 01:37:04.580
Okay, got it!

01:37:09.970 --> 01:37:11.660
The emergency stairs are this way!

01:37:11.660 --> 01:37:12.840
Right.

01:37:14.590 --> 01:37:16.390
Sonoko!

01:37:16.390 --> 01:37:17.740
Who the heck are you?!

01:37:17.740 --> 01:37:19.020
Give us back Ayumi-<i>chan</i>!

01:37:19.020 --> 01:37:21.820
What're you two doing?! Run and hide!

01:37:21.820 --> 01:37:22.630
But...

01:37:22.630 --> 01:37:23.440
He's got Ayumi!

01:37:23.440 --> 01:37:24.980
Get back, you brats!

01:37:26.900 --> 01:37:28.230
No...

01:37:28.230 --> 01:37:29.030
Sonoko!

01:37:29.030 --> 01:37:33.400
Don't cause any trouble, you brats! Just stay where you are!

01:37:33.400 --> 01:37:35.750
I'm gonna borrow this girl!

01:37:36.770 --> 01:37:38.240
Stay back!

01:37:38.240 --> 01:37:41.320
This is the FBI! Drop your gun!

01:37:41.320 --> 01:37:45.810
Shut up! If you come any closer, I'll kill this girl!

01:37:46.900 --> 01:37:48.250
Muzzle flashes...!

01:37:48.250 --> 01:37:50.670
Damn, he <i>still</i> hasn't given up?!

01:37:50.670 --> 01:37:52.920
Don't let him head around the back.

01:37:52.920 --> 01:37:54.680
Bring him this way...

01:37:58.760 --> 01:38:00.220
Stop running around!

01:38:00.220 --> 01:38:02.270
You want me to kill the girl?!

01:38:02.270 --> 01:38:04.230
Drop your guns and let me through!

01:38:02.820 --> 01:38:05.720
All right, we've gotta save Ayumi-<i>chan</i>!

01:38:04.700 --> 01:38:08.540
{BG}Okay! We'll do what you say, so just calm down! {I literally can't hear this at all}

01:38:05.720 --> 01:38:06.550
Right!

01:38:06.550 --> 01:38:09.980
Don't be stupid! He's got a gun!

01:38:09.980 --> 01:38:11.990
But we do have to save her somehow...

01:38:11.990 --> 01:38:14.650
Sonoko! Come on! Sonoko!

01:38:15.730 --> 01:38:18.200
What should I do, Shin'ichi?

01:38:18.200 --> 01:38:19.160
Help me...

01:38:19.160 --> 01:38:22.160
Damn! I can't do anything from down here!

01:38:22.160 --> 01:38:23.850
That's enough!

01:38:23.850 --> 01:38:26.290
Do it now or I'll kill her!

01:38:26.290 --> 01:38:30.710
To ensure successful recovery of hostages, you have to disable the target instantly.

01:38:30.710 --> 01:38:31.840
But to do that...

01:38:31.960 --> 01:38:39.850
There's only one spot where you can kill someone with a single bullet, and cut off all possible convulsions.

01:38:39.890 --> 01:38:41.310
The brain stem...

01:38:41.310 --> 01:38:42.640
Right.

01:38:43.010 --> 01:38:44.810
I have to do it!

01:38:44.810 --> 01:38:47.810
Damn, they won't let me through…

01:38:48.860 --> 01:38:50.440
Jodie-<i>san</i>!

01:38:52.730 --> 01:38:53.900
Yoshino!

01:38:55.570 --> 01:38:56.700
You're mine!

01:39:12.340 --> 01:39:14.340
No! What's going on?!

01:39:14.920 --> 01:39:16.520
I can't see a thing!

01:39:16.520 --> 01:39:17.670
A power cut?!

01:39:17.670 --> 01:39:19.840
Quiet, both of you! Get back!

01:39:22.850 --> 01:39:25.140
Damn! He got the lights!

01:39:25.140 --> 01:39:26.770
Now Subaru-<i>san</i> can't…

01:39:27.670 --> 01:39:28.770
I see.

01:39:28.770 --> 01:39:32.770
He intends to escape under cover of darkness.

01:39:33.570 --> 01:39:34.780
What should I do?

01:39:34.780 --> 01:39:36.070
We're in trouble!

01:39:36.070 --> 01:39:38.320
He'll end up taking Ayumi with him!

01:39:38.320 --> 01:39:39.320
NIGHT VISION MODE

01:39:44.220 --> 01:39:47.410
Don't tell me... Night-vision goggles?!

01:39:47.410 --> 01:39:49.700
Run, Jodie-<i>sensei</i>!

01:39:53.470 --> 01:39:55.760
Yoshino! You can't win, so give up!{lit. Resistance is futile!}

01:39:59.550 --> 01:40:00.970
Camel!

01:40:00.970 --> 01:40:03.380
Say something, Camel!

01:40:03.890 --> 01:40:07.990
Damn it, he's going to kill everyone!

01:40:07.990 --> 01:40:12.980
If I can just shine light on him somehow, Subaru-<i>san</i> should be able to snipe him.

01:40:13.070 --> 01:40:15.480
But I can't support myself with my leg like this!

01:40:16.190 --> 01:40:18.830
How can I let him see Yoshino?

01:40:19.040 --> 01:40:22.660
Hold on! Those night-vision goggles are old style ones...

01:40:23.080 --> 01:40:27.580
That means I just have to shine light on the Bell Tree!

01:40:27.580 --> 01:40:28.750
How about that?!

01:40:29.930 --> 01:40:33.240
If I use this height, it might work!

01:40:33.240 --> 01:40:36.420
No, it <i>has</i> to work!

01:40:39.420 --> 01:40:40.920
Edogawa-<i>kun</i>?

01:40:40.920 --> 01:40:41.900
Hello?

01:40:41.900 --> 01:40:45.050
Light! Shine light on the sniper!

01:40:45.420 --> 01:40:48.470
He's wearing night-vision goggles. It'll blind him!

01:40:48.470 --> 01:40:50.790
But where is he...?

01:40:51.120 --> 01:40:52.870
Right. Use that.

01:40:52.870 --> 01:40:53.810
Got it.

01:40:53.810 --> 01:40:55.690
He'll be passing by you soon.

01:40:55.690 --> 01:40:58.990
Don't move for thirty seconds, so he doesn't get suspicious.

01:40:58.990 --> 01:41:00.490
I'm hanging up!

01:41:00.490 --> 01:41:04.160
Listen. You have to stay perfectly still for the next thirty seconds!

01:41:04.610 --> 01:41:05.410
Sure!

01:41:12.920 --> 01:41:15.170
I'll get one more chance.

01:41:15.680 --> 01:41:17.920
I can count on that boy...

01:41:19.170 --> 01:41:20.920
Please, let this work...

01:41:21.660 --> 01:41:22.840
You ready?

01:41:22.840 --> 01:41:24.620
Right!

01:41:25.020 --> 01:41:26.100
Here goes!

01:41:36.270 --> 01:41:39.000
Where is it?! Where's it coming from?!

01:41:39.000 --> 01:41:40.280
Hold on!

01:41:45.570 --> 01:41:46.650
Over there!

01:41:46.650 --> 01:41:47.200
All right!

01:41:47.200 --> 01:41:48.700
Here goes!

01:41:50.290 --> 01:41:50.700
Now!

01:41:51.830 --> 01:41:52.710
What?!

01:41:57.300 --> 01:41:58.960
Yoshida-<i>san</i>, over here!

01:42:02.510 --> 01:42:04.510
Ai-<i>chan</i>!

01:42:04.510 --> 01:42:07.430
You dumb brats!

01:42:07.800 --> 01:42:10.220
Everybody run!

01:42:10.730 --> 01:42:11.640
Ran-<i>san</i>!

01:42:11.640 --> 01:42:13.810
Stop, Ran!

01:42:22.940 --> 01:42:24.220
Ran!

01:42:24.220 --> 01:42:26.950
Damn! I can't just sit here!

01:42:31.330 --> 01:42:33.830
What should I do, Shin'ichi?

01:42:40.600 --> 01:42:42.290
You had to try and be a hero...

01:42:42.290 --> 01:42:43.710
Now I've got a new hostage.

01:42:45.840 --> 01:42:46.980
It's now or never...

01:42:46.980 --> 01:42:48.220
I've got to do this!

01:42:48.220 --> 01:42:49.720
Just hold on...

01:42:51.000 --> 01:42:52.720
Ran!

01:43:24.920 --> 01:43:27.590
Go!

01:43:35.100 --> 01:43:35.980
Now!

01:43:42.770 --> 01:43:43.770
Hmph...

01:43:50.510 --> 01:43:51.450
What?!

01:43:52.160 --> 01:43:53.330
What is that?!

01:44:10.840 --> 01:44:11.840
Ran!

01:44:16.270 --> 01:44:17.850
This is for Sonoko!

01:44:21.020 --> 01:44:23.810
And Ayumi-<i>chan</i>!

01:44:29.320 --> 01:44:32.740
And Sera-<i>san</i>!

01:44:42.180 --> 01:44:44.670
Right. We've secured Yoshino!

01:44:47.170 --> 01:44:48.490
That was great!

01:44:48.490 --> 01:44:50.480
You were amazing, Ran-<i>san</i>!

01:44:50.480 --> 01:44:51.260
Ran!

01:44:51.910 --> 01:44:53.150
Sonoko!

01:44:53.150 --> 01:44:54.510
That was so cool, Ran!

01:44:55.510 --> 01:44:58.150
Are you feeling okay, Sonoko?

01:44:58.150 --> 01:45:01.020
I have no idea what's going on, but I'm perfectly fine!

01:45:01.020 --> 01:45:04.860
Huh? Wait, why are the lights out? Was there a power cut...?

01:45:04.860 --> 01:45:07.020
Oh, Sonoko...

01:45:12.180 --> 01:45:15.540
Damn, she's relentless...

01:45:16.030 --> 01:45:20.180
Target silenced. All clear.

01:45:20.320 --> 01:45:26.500
Right. I just heard from Jodie-<i>kun</i>. Good work. I'll be in contact again.

01:45:31.020 --> 01:45:32.540
Roger.

01:45:34.470 --> 01:45:41.020
I've been slowly searching for you with my one steady beam of light

01:45:34.470 --> 01:45:41.020
yurari egaita light de sotto kimi no koto sagashita yo

01:45:34.470 --> 01:45:41.020
yurari egaita light de sotto kimi no koto sagashita yo

01:45:41.020 --> 01:45:45.770
I'll keep shining upon you with my invisible light of love

